{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility","id":1444503,"title":"Can someone explain to me the Syndicate paradigm of Primal Utility?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-18T07:48:55-07:00","id":1444503,"title":"Can someone explain to me the Syndicate paradigm of Primal Utility?","content":"And, in fact, start telling me how exactly the Technocracy and the Syndicate deals with most magic at all? <br /> <br /> Like, let's say that according to the M20 Book of Secrets rules that a person out in the field realizes that he's in dire need of a source of Agg damage for a bunch of super-fast healing combat homunculi made by an Etherite. He's got a good knife on him, and he's decided to use it on them. He's got Prime 3, and fully capable of making a Talisman... <br /> <br /> But here's the thing: What's the paradigmatic justification for being able to have an ordinary knife inflict Agg damage when previously it was a normal knife? What does he exactly do? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Through sophisticated uses of instruments and principles... hypereconomist can... create something from nothing... use the normal prime 2 effects, although the character still needs to have some technological source to facilitate his conjurations. </div> </div> </div>So what does he use? Does he buy a particularly expensive knife sharpener or special alloy and cover the knife with it? <br /> <br /> Actually, I've been looking at M20 and it's seemingly odder and odder. What's the paradigmatic justification for a lot of the stuff the Technocracy can do? I mean, Matter 2 lets you carry out transmutation. Not a lot, but it's there, even when it breaks the laws of atoms. What's the paradigm justification in the Technocracy that lets them carry out transmutation without a nuclear reactor, or is the Technocracy simply locked out of effects like this? <br /> <br /> Did the order of reason be able to transmute metals in the start? In Technocracy labs, do they have specialized machines that let them create near anything, but cannot be brought out of the lab due to sheer vulgarity of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:38:50-07:00","id":1444509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility#post1444503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the paradigm justification in the Technocracy that lets them carry out transmutation without a nuclear reactor, or is the Technocracy simply locked out of effects like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>your Amalgam doesn\u2019t keep a travel size cold fusion reaction chamber on hand? That\u2019s a basic need for an Enlightened Chemist (Matter Adept).<br /> <br /> As for pairing Prime Utility to create something from nothing - you\u2019re literally converting the potential energy of human ingenuity and desire into matter, so it\u2019s highly vulgar, but the tech to do it would look something like a Star Trek replicator. Though if that aesthetic doesn\u2019t appeal, you could make it look more like a 3D printer, just without material plastics, it\u2019s converting said energy into matter in its construction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Using these in the field would indeed result in Statistical Inevitability eventually outside the controllable environment of the lab (radiation burns from your fusion reactor, your replicator creates and releases something it shouldn\u2019t have, etc etc), but such is the price of the bleeding edge of Enlightened Science","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-18-2021, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T11:20:37-07:00","id":1444525,"title":"","content":"Most of the time, the Technocracy does indeed require a much larger amount of Instruments to be on hand in order to perform miraculous feats than a follower of a Mystic Paradigm might. It's explicitly built into their mechanics not allowing them to discard as many Instruments through raised Arete, at least according to M20. But you can do a surprising amount if you imagine your Instrument to be a super-tech wonder-gadget. I don't watch Doctor Who, but the &quot;sonic screwdriver&quot; is often held up as an example.<br /> <br /> To get a bit more extreme, the Technocratic Paradigm does leave some room for Psionics. Once you gather the Energy with Primal Utility, you use your psychic abilities to create a conduit that channels the Energy into your knife-blade, then a force-field of sorts to contain it there.<br /> <br /> Edit: that bit about accepting Psionics is also kind of how they handle &quot;magic&quot; in general. It's not &quot;magic,&quot; it's Psionic powers that the Reality Deviants focus through ignorant superstition because they lack the Enlightenment necessary to truly understand the Rational Scientific Principles that *obviously* explain all of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-18-2021, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:31:34-07:00","id":1444550,"title":"","content":"With a lot of what the Syndicate does, you can excuse a great deal just by appending a high pricetag to it. Syndicate reps believe - strongly - in the power of money, and in the principle that &quot;you get what you pay for&quot;.<br /> <br /> If they pull out a knife and use a Prime 2 Effect to make it magickally charged, it could be as simple as the character dwelling on the fact they paid top dollar for that knife. It's probably a special knife, manufactured in a lab, at great expense. Regardless of whether the knife itself genuinely has any special properties, the Syndicate's belief in the efficacy of money will allow them to get more out of the knife than an unEnlightened person could.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of Sphere abilities are more the upper limit of what Spheres can do at a given level. The real determiner of a Mage's abilities is what they believe is possible within their Focus. This includes what Instruments are required, which can be as broad or as specific as the Player/Storyteller wants. This is why the Syndicate rep would need to have the specially manufactured knife to do the Prime 2 Effect, rather than any old knife they bought from a store. Or at the very least, they'd need to visit a high-end hardware, kitchen supply, or weapons shop to get a knife of sufficient quality (read: price). Rather than just picking up a box cutter or piece of cutlery from the dollar store.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the subject of making stuff from nothing, the Syndicate have another &quot;cheat&quot; they can employ that's part of their Paradigm: they can &quot;find&quot; items they require. The world around us can be full of hidden compartments, that a savvy Syndicate rep can &quot;open&quot; with the right knowledge, to reveal &quot;caches&quot; of useful equipment. If those things didn't otherwise exist, the Syndicate character won't call attention to that.<br /> <br /> Syndicate reps also tend to be well-connected, with networks of resources and people ready to do their bidding or make things happen. If they need a gun, for instance, they might ring someone up, ordering one to be delivered. If the item arrives through the mail, by courier, in a drop box, or arriving from the sky via a delivery drone or parachuting drop container (ala Metal Gear Solid V: The Phantom Pain). Is there a place where these items first entered the supply chain? Or did they appear within it when no one was looking, just in time to find its way into the Syndicate rep's waiting hands? Who can say.<br /> <br /> (Obviously, this is all very borderline Results Based Determinism, rather than Process Based Determinism. Although at least with sufficient Matter, you could argue part of the Effect is doing the material changes to the environment for as long as it takes to pick the item up. Although if you can't see the inside of a mailbox, what Hypothetical Average Witness could say if it didn't have a package arrive at some point before the Scene began? Reality doesn't seem to care as much about how long ago something was checked, so long as it wasn't observed shortly before. It's the same reason why Mages can teleport a gun into their pocket from elsewhere.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:06:41-07:00","id":1444555,"title":"","content":"I have a Syndicate member who secretly has a bit of a &quot;mystical&quot; bent. He believes in what he terms the &quot;Inherent Value Principle (IVP).&quot; That money is the only value in the universe. Not just US dollars, or yen, of whatever. It's the value placed upon it that makes it valuable. If it were cupcakes, then cupcakes would be a source of Primal Utility, and in fact are at bakeries known for them. <br /> When he performs vulgar Enlightened Science he is exchanging the value he has built up, either with actual money, or whatever, and he is sending out a commission request to the IVP, this allows potentiality, worth, value, and Quintessence to warp what he needs done.<br /> He turns in that value, makes a request for his desire, and then hopes he exchanged enough worth to safely receive his desire. If not then he'll have to suffer from the Market taking it's due, Market Adjustment.<br /> Then again, if he gets caught doing some of the things he does, NWO might bring him in for some conditioning.<br /> Just remember what you can really do in reality with large sums of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:54:16-07:00","id":1444559,"title":"","content":"Also, if it doesn't make sense in your paradigm, you can't do it. You're allowed to bend over backward trying to make a rationale for something, but if you aren't up to the task of doing so, then tough.<br /> <br /> This is true for everyone, not just Technocrats. <br /> <br /> Note, however, that the explanation doesn't have to make sense to Sleepers; <i>that's</i> only required if you want the Effect to be Coincidental. Most Technocrats can get away with \u201cHypertechnology\u201d as a justification for what they do, of they're willing to pay the price in Paradox. Syndics are the exception: they pride themselves in avoiding Vulgar Magick whenever possible; and as such, you're far more likely to encounter situations where they'll \u201ctake the loss\u201d rather than do something that would potentially trigger a Backlash. When they start breaking out the hypertech, that's when you know that they're getting desperate.<br /> <br /> In addition, TR suggests that technocrats tend to rely much more heavily on Wonders than the Superstitionists do \u2014 mainly because they have a larger supply of them. There's a reason why Requisitions is Technocrat only: they're the only faction in the Ascension War that's got a large enough stockpile of Wonders for said Background to make any sense. The way I play them, what Instruments they have tend to be very complicated but multi-purpose; and working Procedures or Adjustments on the fly essentially boils down to calibrating these broadly useful tools for a specific purpose. Not quite as general purpose as a Sonic Screwdriver, but that's the sort of idea. It's only when you get into Coincidental Effects that the Technocrat starts to require a lot of special purpose Instruments.<br /> <br /> Even there, though, I tend to run Technocrats using a variation of the Trinity Continuum's Dramatic Editing: the player of a Technocrat doesn't have to specify precisely what she's carrying, just a general idea of the sorts of Instruments (and Wonders, if she has Requisitions) on hand. If she needs something in the field that may not fit the profile of her general loadout, she can make a Coincidental Enlightenment roll to see if she has it or finds it lying around. (The type of Feat, i.e. number of required successes, depends on how absurd the request is.)<br /> <br /> I generally don't allow Psionics unless the Technocrat in question has specified Psionics as part of his Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T16:02:02-07:00","id":1444561,"title":"","content":"In terms of making something out of nothing, that tends to go against The Syndicate Focus. So you're generally won't see much of it. For the most part, Syndics use Primal utility to gather Primal energy and to make Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T16:14:36-07:00","id":1444564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444559#post1444559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't allow Psionics unless the Technocrat in question has specified Psionics as part of his Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed, just mentioning that it is an option on the table, since this seems to be more of a hypothetical than an actual character with a specific Focus that needs a specific answer. Psionics in the Syndicate would be extremely unusual. In generally they are heavily monitored even when they are present in the Technocracy, from my understanding; probably have mountains of Conditioning, and possibly even some kind of self-destruct implant that can be used against them if they go rogue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T18:56:15-07:00","id":1444585,"title":"","content":"Mostly, they're found in the New World Order and in the Void Engineers (think \u201cTrinity Continuum: \u00c6on\u201d: the whole of it for the Void Engineers, and the Ministry and ISRA for the NWO). That said, I could see Iteration X doing a \u201cmechanically telepathy\u201d type of thing, where brain implants with radio transponders allow the Convention to network brains together the way we network computers (and electrokinetics/cyberpsi and telekinesis would intrigue them); and the Progenitors might be working on Psionics as part of a Human Upgrade package (as well as being fascinated with the biokinetic stuff). <br /> <br /> There probably <i>are</i> a lot of Technocrats who practice Psionics, actually. A <i>minority</i>; and they kept their heads down around Sleepers. But they're there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:15:12-07:00","id":1444655,"title":"","content":"Oh i came up with an exemple of what a syndicate would do in a house with only the most ordinary knives. Since syndicate is all about Value, as stat3d above, to make it have agg damage all you would need is to raise the knife value, or &quot;worthness&quot;, but how? Simple you just need to discard or destroy all the other knives, the reamining one is the only one, the unique object to carry the simbolical value of a knife and its potenticial and necessity. Since the value is exceeded it becomes capable of what a generic object cant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:00:24-07:00","id":1444667,"title":"","content":"Another option, especially with the throw money at the issue paradigm, is that an online order and drone delivery can get you most things you need, and you can always pay more for <i>super express delivery</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:51:34-07:00","id":1444669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444667#post1444667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option, especially with the throw money at the issue paradigm, is that an online order and drone delivery can get you most things you need, and you can always pay more for <i>super express delivery</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pay a million dollars for a rocket launcher in a remote cave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:58:41-07:00","id":1444672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444669#post1444669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pay a million dollars for a rocket launcher in a remote cave?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pay a million dollars for someone in a Technocrat Construct to teleport a rocket launcher into your hands, since they can convert those dollars into Quintessence, or even more mundane resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:22:54-07:00","id":1444834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-