":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:55:47-07:00","id":1444944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444939#post1444939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Process &gt; Results Based Determinism, in my books. The teleportation being &quot;off screen&quot; is irrelevant for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned that I had the idea that a Syndicate Matter rote would be paying someone to construct a building overnight and somehow they'd get it done.<br /> <br /> A guy I talked to said that made no sense and wasn't real magic and was stupid among other descriptors.<br /> <br /> I said, &quot;What matters is the building is there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:11:31-07:00","id":1444948,"title":"","content":"It's a perfect example of the Human Resources instrument in action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:34:04-07:00","id":1444953,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but that (by itself) wouldn't make it any less Vulgar than screaming &quot;Abracadabra&quot;, and the building making itself overningth.<br /> <br /> PBD, the stance of M20, says that the &quot;how&quot; it's important. But in the example of the building, even w/o PBD it's important for the matter of Vulgarity:<br /> <br /> What exactly would an external observer see, if the observer get's into the premise? - this observer doesn't even need to be hypotetical, this is a very real risk in a populated place.<br /> <br /> You could say you use magick or something to make sure nobody sees - that would be straining HAP to the point of absurdity: The point where anything it's going to be Coincident as long as you can turn off the ligth or place a blanket over it (exactly the criticism that HAP detractors have).<br /> <br /> To make such a thing Coincident, under M20 at least, you would need to go an *extra mile*. The extra mile of making people think such a thing it's feasible (like in the Prime 2 &quot;3d print&quot; above - w/o some knowledgeable skeptic carefully dismantling the machine, how can you know it's not just a 3d print?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:45:44-07:00","id":1444956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444929#post1444929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the Syndicate is that their paradigm is the same as the rest of the Unions but they use mathematics, credit, and resource allocation to maximize the efficiency of creation.<br /> <br /> I state that they're the closest to the Virtual Adepts in terms of how they think but instead of information=Reality, they believe value=reality.<br /> <br /> I imagine if you explained their views to Progenitors or Iteration X, however, both would go ballistic.<br /> <br /> But I always remember Enlightened Scientists are still Mages and their views are still going to sound insane to Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> With PU 5 a Syndicate agent can bankrupt someone so hard, that someone will just cease to exist. That doesn't make sense?, well neither does erasing someone's &quot;code&quot; like if ppl were programs. Mages believe in weird shit.<br /> <br /> Even those not of the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> It's important to always say this mantra: &quot;Technocracy isn't about real science&quot;. Technocracy knows what they do isn't normal - that's why they call it &quot;enligthened science&quot;. They believe (and they're not entirely wrong) to be in possesion of secrets normal scientists can't possibly fathom, that real sciense it's...not necessarily <i>wrong, </i>per se, but incomplete and shallow - if your Instruments allows to do something science says it's impossible (as ALL Instruments do at some point), that just proves a limitation of normal sciences.<br /> <br /> How they do transmute w/o a nuclear reactor?: Well, fortunately they have their trusty sonic emmiter that can vibrate stuff - usually this would just break the stuff, but with the rigth application of science you can alter the atomic structure of the thing with those vibrations<br /> <br /> Too absurd for the Technocracy? - I'm willing to bet I can find 3 canon Technocratic foci that are more absurd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:49:16-07:00","id":1444957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444953#post1444953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, but that (by itself) wouldn't make it any less Vulgar than screaming &quot;Abracadabra&quot;, and the building making itself overningth.<br /> <br /> PBD, the canon stance of M20, says that the &quot;how&quot; it's important. But in the example of the building, even w/o PBD it's important for the matter of Vulgarity: What exactly would an external observer see, if the observer get's into the premise? - this observer doesn't even need to be hypotetical, this is a very real risk in a populated place.<br /> <br /> You could say you use magick or something to make sure nobody sees - that would be straining HAP to the point of absurdity: The point where anything it's going to be Coincident as long as you can turn off the ligth or place a blanket over it (exactly the criticism that HAP detractors have).<br /> <br /> To make such a thing Coincident, under M20 at least, you would need to go an *extra mile*. The extra mile of making people think such a thing it's feasible (like in the Prime 2 &quot;3d print&quot; above - w/o some knowledgeable skeptic carefully dismantling the machine, how can you know it's not just a 3d print?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I'd imagine the workers working are the reason it would be coincidental even if it would be absurdly fast that it was made overnight. The Syndicate's foci are necessary because they're Technocracts but that doesn't mean that they're what actually makes it happen.<br /> <br /> One of the 2nd Edition examples was that a guy drove a car without an engine to a garage and then left before they checked to see that the car had no engine.<br /> <br /> It didn't generate paradox because it was after the affect had happened, no matter how confusing it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:51:21-07:00","id":1444958,"title":"","content":"As written, if Human resources works at all, it's coincidental. That is, you're not allowed to use it on vulgar effects. In this example, it works because the construction team is incredibly efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:52:12-07:00","id":1444959,"title":"","content":"I must admit, using the word &quot;magic&quot; does strike me as rather odd when describing extremely mundane uses of Human Resources and such as an Instrument. But I kind of imagine it as their Will influencing, enhancing, streamlining the set of mundane processes involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:18:04-07:00","id":1444965,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, yes.<br /> <br /> As I said in my first post here, Syndics are suspected by many of not actually being mages. They are, but extreme distaste for the vulgar stuff makes many question whether anything they do is actually magic. The human resources thing is one such example of that.<br /> <br /> Their other preferred instruments are things like accessing hidden features of otherwise mundane technology and or having technology that's \u201cpremium\u201d, doing what the regular model would do except better; doing the same with one's own skills, knowledge's, and talents (Syndics are very much into being the best that they can be), and spending money in ways that don't actually work in reality (such as writing a check to buy a restaurant on the spot, just so you can boss the staff around). They try <i>not</i> to do things like making stuff appear out of thin air. But as I said a few posts back, they could do it using a 3D printer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:24:56-07:00","id":1444966,"title":"","content":"Basically, Syndics aren't exactly Frontline troop material. Where they really shine is when they're a mastermind running things from behind the scenes. Despite not being all that notable on a street fight, the technocracy is arguably what it is today largely because of them: their Primal ventures ensure that the technocracy has all the quintessence that you could want, and I would argue that the technocracies ability to make gadgets without having to spend willpower is a syndicate innovation.: Small things that have huge impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:28:49-07:00","id":1444969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444959#post1444959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit, using the word &quot;magic&quot; does strike me as rather odd when describing extremely mundane uses of Human Resources and such as an Instrument. But I kind of imagine it as their Will influencing, enhancing, streamlining the set of mundane processes involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidental Time, Prime, and Entropy effects I assume.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the thing about Prime magic would be that if you use it, you would have access to the resources in the Syndicate's paradigm no matter where you were and how.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate rote is not winning the lottery, it is rigging it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:39:34-07:00","id":1444972,"title":"","content":"I'd look at Bruce Wayne, Tony Stark, and David Xanatos as examples of a Syndic at work. In particular, see Bruce's \u201cprep time\u201d and the \u201cXanatos Gambit\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:09:50-07:00","id":1445003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444969#post1444969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coincidental Time, Prime, and Entropy effects I assume.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the thing about Prime magic would be that if you use it, you would have access to the resources in the Syndicate's paradigm no matter where you were and how.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate rote is not winning the lottery, it is rigging it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the primary 'power' of the Syndicate Primal Utility is that it doesn't really matte where the heck you are. In fact, it barely recognizes it. You can't charge a credit card on a node. What it means is that Syndicate members have to go out into human society and do things, not cloister themselves in a monastery. They have to start investing in human society, whether that's a trading corporation, a chain of shops, or a bunch of flower sellers. Guess who got more popular? <br /> <br /> On the thinking of the Syndicate and 'making a building in one night' I would say that it's something that's rather vulgar. A build-time that's incredibly fast and smooth with no red tape, able to make it in a month when it would normally take a year? Possible. But overnight? That requires things. Hot-dropping of high level equipment from Iteration X. Holographic emitters to prevent Sleeper Witnesses. Stimulants and nootropics for the workers and supervisors, for tireless work, coordination, and motivation. And a substantial bonus for making such a great and good thing. <br /> <br /> And of course, there's the backlash or market corrections. Workers fall to their deaths because there's no time to set up safety nets. High powered equipment causes collateral damage and injuries. Overwork causes worker hearts to explode and livers to fail. Or maybe the structure collapses because you just rushed the work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:47:02-07:00","id":1445029,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Using Human Resources to make a building <i><b>overnight </b></i>- if possible -it's most likely going to be Vulgar: What exactly would an external observer see?<br /> <br /> &quot;Workers working&quot; it's not a good enough explanation if the workers need to be working like a fast foward movie, with suff just appearing in their hands when they need it, in order to accomplish the feat.<br /> <br /> Time would make it look like a fast foward movie - Vulgar.<br /> <br /> If it materializes stuff with Prime, most likely would be Vulgar - 3D printing would be useless here, because printing stuff in a &quot;coincidental way&quot; it's going to be slower than just having the materials be sent in trucks prior to make the building, like normal ppl does. (and the Syndicate it's smart enough to make *this* process go faster)<br /> <br /> Adding Entropy making things run smoothly wouldn't be enough to make it &quot;overnigth&quot;<br /> <br /> But I think it should be feasible, even when the Syndicate most likely wouldn't do it. The Syndicate would build in half the time it normaly takes with the amount of resources at hand, perhaps 1/3 of the time. Because those are the limits of Time and coincidence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-21-2021, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T06:01:09-07:00","id":1445033,"title":"","content":"Or, in other words:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444957#post1444957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, I'd imagine the workers working are the reason it would be coincidental even if it would be absurdly fast that it was made overnight.<br /> <br /> One of the 2nd Edition examples was that a guy drove a car without an engine to a garage and then left before they checked to see that the car had no engine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the workers *look* like they're working absurdly fast, then it's Vulgar.<br /> <br /> The car example uses HAP to make it Coincident because normal bystanders don't know how your car it's geared, and can't know it w/o opening the car. And cars tend to move. But bystanders *do* tend to look at building sites, and buildings *don't* tend to appear overnigth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Odd&quot; does matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T06:31:54-07:00","id":1445038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444965#post1444965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their other preferred instruments are things like accessing hidden features of otherwise mundane technology</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I've always found odd<br /> <br /> A) Under PBD, you need extra successes to actually *make* every aspect of the hidden feature. Yet this is usually mentioned <i>even in M20</i> as part of the focus and not part of the effect...<br /> <br /> More so: I get you believe in &quot;the man&quot; placing stuff everywhere, but: what's the actual <i>instrument</i> here?, &quot;any stuff I can get my hands on&quot; counts as an instrument? - I seem to remember you have to declare your 7 Instruments, you can't just invent new instruments on the fly (there are rules to add more, unfamiliar, instruments).<br /> <br /> I think Technocrats are often struggling to use Instruments - yet they need to do so, thus the books bend over backwards to try making them not as impractical as other mages by glossig over *how* they actually make this kind of stuff happen.<br /> But I think you should declare your agent knows the &quot;hidden Illuminatus paswords of the modern world&quot;, or whatever you use to pull stuff out of stuff, at chargen to be able to do it (w/o the unfamiliar instrument penalty). Also that should be part of a Practice and a Paradigm, like with any magic word<br /> <br /> B) This is described as &quot;extreme distaste for the vulgar stuff &quot;, as if it was more coincident than making it out of &quot;thin air&quot;. But, is it?, is it really?<br /> <br /> Forget for a moment about the Technocracy. Would you believe a Microsoft goon can grab your laptop and pull a hidden gun out of it? - because I would believe I'm in a weird dream if something like that happened. Same if a &quot;hidden door&quot; oppened in a wall of my house to allow the entrance of someone with a suit...<br /> <br /> It is better than the gun literally &quot;appearing from nowhere&quot;, but not by a whole lot. Like, taking out a handerchief and making a gun appear under it wouldn't be <i>more </i>unbelievable in my opinion. Ultimately both depend on ppl believing in tricks and illusions, stuff not being what it seems<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it &quot;magic&quot;, but I wouldn't call it magic when a Hermetic pulls a want and makes a ball of fire appear out of it either (I would believe the wand has a hidden flamethrower instead), and, on the scale of &quot;impossible to believe&quot;, I would place the &quot;hidden door in my house&quot; above the fireball, really, and the hidden gun next to it (summoning flames from a wand show &quot;an extreme distaste for the vulgar stuff&quot;, now?).<br /> <br /> I can get an agent believes the Technocracy it's everywhere (and &quot;of course&quot; they added a hidden door/gun), but normal people should be very weirded by this kind of things happening, shouldn't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-21-2021, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:30:07-07:00","id":1445071,"title":"","content":"Rather than workers moving in fast forward, I would handle it as an extreme version of <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_and_motion_study\" target=\"_blank\">time-motion study</a>: no individual action by anyone is supernaturally fast; but there isn't a wasted motion anywhere, and the crew operates in concert like a well choreographed dance. So the job gets done incredibly fast.<br /> <br /> Now, I wouldn't expect this to work with, say, a crew of five people. Note would I expect it to work if you grab a bunch of random people off the street. You need enough manpower for the task at hand, and they need to be competent at the task. Using Management and Human Resources merely results in them being more efficient. Likewise, you'll need to apply them with the materials to do their job. <br /> <br /> If you're talking about having a building literally appear out of nowhere, well, that's not something the Syndicate does. TANSTAAFL. You need to put the money, material, manpower, and time into the space to construct the building; what their Magick can do is to streamline the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T11:18:38-07:00","id":1445080,"title":"","content":"Slightly incorrect. The syndicate can do it... it's just vulgar. And can get you knocks on the door. <br /> <br /> &quot;What the fuck, Financier? How did you set this up? Did you use reality deviancy?&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Nonsense, Operative. I simply decided to pay a premium... and the Market chose to provide.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:11:20-07:00","id":1445091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445071#post1445071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than workers moving in fast forward, I would handle it as an extreme version of <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_and_motion_study\" target=\"_blank\">time-motion study</a>: no individual action by anyone is supernaturally fast; but there isn't a wasted motion anywhere, and the crew operates in concert like a well choreographed dance. So the job gets done incredibly fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. That's a very good example - but it misses my point<br /> <br /> My point was: There's a limit how fast can something be accomplished before it's Vulgar. Usually that's twice, perhaps trice, as fast as normal (the same limits apply to any other Time mage) - in general this is how it get's described in the books.<br /> <br /> Of course, that depends on how cinematic you think reality is - but that is hardly a function of Syndicate paradigm, but your own preconceptions of what's Vulgar and what isn't.<br /> <br /> M20 states you can do one or two extra actions before asceleration becomes Vulgar (framing it as &quot; time&amp;motion management&quot; doesn't help - the exerpt from Time it's Instrument agnostic, it <i>assumes </i>you're doing something to make it look normal and not someone moving like a fast foward video), hence why I suggest &quot;twice or thrice faster&quot; - an argument can be made about being more flexible, but ultimately that would be besides the point.<br /> <br /> I do think, being more flexible with the definitions, that you could build overnight with pure time&amp;motion what a top efficient mundane with the same resources would take two or three days of nonstop work. 100% Coincident. But there's a point where it's so fast it becomes Vulgar, no matter your Instrument.<br /> <br /> For instance: If you want to, say, do <i>overnight </i>what the extremely efficient chinese goverment can do in a week (build a big hospital), <i>with their same resources</i>: That would require more than <b>x14 </b>speed (or time&amp;motion or whatever you want to call it) - that's a LOT more than the proposed limits to Coincidence, and in general a LOT more than anything believable. Well, I say that's Vulgar rigtht there and WOULD look like a fast foward movie (or some other bizarre thing, like what Accelerator suggested) no matter how much you want to finesse it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-21-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:19:59-07:00","id":1445095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445038#post1445038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something I've always found odd<br /> <br /> A) Under PBD, you need extra successes to actually *make* every aspect of the hidden feature. Yet this is usually mentioned <i>even in M20</i> as part of the focus and not part of the effect...<br /> <br /> More so: I get you believe in &quot;the man&quot; placing stuff everywhere, but: what's the actual <i>instrument</i> here?, &quot;any stuff I can get my hands on&quot; counts as an instrument? - I seem to remember you have to declare your 7 Instruments, you can't just invent new instruments on the fly (there are rules to add more, unfamiliar, instruments).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two different but similar looking things that can be happening here:<br /> <br /> The Technocrat could know there are hidden features in a lot of things. The feature is actually there already and waiting to be used. It is a focus, not an effect.<br /> <br /> The Technocrat could &quot;know&quot; there are hidden features in a lot of things. There's not, though, he's actually unconsciously casting. This is an effect, not a focus.<br /> <br /> I don't think either runs afoul of the 7 instruments unless we are artificially specific about instruments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Technocrats are often struggling to use Instruments - yet they need to do so, thus the books bend over backwards to try making them not as impractical as other mages by glossig over *how* they actually make this kind of stuff happen. </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. A lot of paradigms struggle to operate timely. Preparing components, sigils, mathematics, etc. often takes a lot of time and it is assumed Mages do much of it off screen so that they can cast on the fly when they need to. This really isn't that different.<br /> <br /> And yeah, pulling a gun out of a random computer is going to be pretty Vulgar. This is a power best used coincidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T13:00:14-07:00","id":1445106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445095#post1445095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocrat could know there are hidden features in a lot of things. The feature is actually there already and waiting to be used. It is a focus, not an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this as one Instrument: &quot;spy gadgets&quot;, or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocrat could &quot;know&quot; there are hidden features in a lot of things. There's not, though, he's actually unconsciously casting. This is an effect, not a focus. </div> </div> </div>But, in this case: Where is the focus?<br /> <br /> A focus would be nedded to cast the effect, wouldn't it?. Technocrats can't cast w/o Instruments. A password, gesture, ID or something has to be included in the list of Instruments to make this &quot;casting&quot; feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:35:08-07:00","id":1445123,"title":"","content":"Syndicate paradigm <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=1xZFeh4kHeY\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=1xZFeh4kHeY</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T04:32:38-07:00","id":1445253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445106#post1445106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the focus?<br /> <br /> A focus would be nedded to cast the effect, wouldn't it?. Technocrats can't cast w/o Instruments. A password, gesture, ID or something has to be included in the list of Instruments to make this &quot;casting&quot; feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I had to put it into words I would call it Analytics.<br /> <br /> In the other scenario we've seen Technocrats cast without realizing it they essentially analyze their surroundings and &quot;realize&quot; that a structural collapse or some other convenient event is about to happen. &quot;The Reality Deviant doesn't realize it but his reckless actions have damaged the support beam and the roof is about to fall on him...&quot; That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> I would say something similar is happening with the &quot;conveniently&quot; seeded technology. The Agent sees a couple of reality deviants conspiring near a fuse box. He &quot;scans&quot; the box and realizes it happens to have a seeded microphone he can use to listen in.<br /> <br /> This is one of those cases where the Mage's own sense of believability plays an important role. Since the Technocrat doesn't realize he is casting, what he thinks he could reasonably find will limit what he can find. It's not really a Vulgar vs Coincidental thing, so much as what he would even consider looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-22-2021, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T06:40:19-07:00","id":1445259,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm sold on that.<br /> <br /> I find it funny you mention:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> n the other scenario we've seen Technocrats cast without realizing it they essentially analyze their surroundings and &quot;realize&quot; that a structural collapse or some other convenient event is about to happen. </div> </div> </div>Because, if my memory doesn't fail: that wasn't originally a <i>focus</i>, but rather was mentioned in an older technocracy book as a special rule to &quot;balance&quot; Traditionalists casting w/o focus.<br /> <br /> It's clever to combine both into one Instrument for M20.<br /> <br /> One could ask: why would anyone have &quot;spy gadgets&quot;, as above, if Analitics does everything and more w/o needing actual material stuff? But that's a problem gadgets have in general as a focus. Also, thanks to &quot;process based determinism&quot;, I imagine having an actual machine may lower the successes needed in some occasions (so, there's that) <hr />Let's note that, as an Instrument,it still needs to be declared. If your Syndic hasn't Analitics declared, he prob can still use it but with the penalty for an unfamiliar instrument.<br /> <br /> Now I wonder what Practices are good for this Instrument...I imagine the kind of lies you can tell to yourself would vary depending on the Practice.<br /> <br /> Hypereconomics it's all about using social constructs to make your will. Prob. it's able to frame this &quot;analisis&quot; as the advantages of being part of a global conspiration, making them able to find all sorts of features or convinient flaws into things, as long as those things are related to the economical umbrella of the Technocracy - knowing that the Technocracy really does add hidden features to items sometimes, but regardless if the actual item actually has them<br /> <br /> I would say that the very real <i>posibility </i>of the item being a gadget it's <i>actualized</i> by the power of Art of Desire. Turning potential into a fact. You prob. know that not all knifes are Technocracy gadgets, but the one you're grabing has to be, thus it is (As Lupin would say: It's possible, thus a fact).<br /> <br /> But I imagine you would need some reason to believe that the stuff it's or could be part of the social constructs that constitute the base of your Art of Desire to take advantage of Analytics that way. In a sense, it's &quot;Faith in the Technocracy&quot; (or similar conspirations) used as a focus.<br /> <br /> It would be unlikely to have Focus in the woods, and knowing the Etherite made his own car (from the raw materials) would ruin your day (<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/memepediadankmemes/images/5/5b/That_Sign_Can%27t_Stop_Me_Because_I_Can%27t_Read.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20180721083144\" target=\"_blank\">but *not* knowing this migth allow you to have Focus?</a>)<br /> <br /> Hypertech, on the other hand, can prob Analize all sorts of flaws (or seeing potential) into mundane tech, but I'm not so sure about &quot;finding&quot; gadgets rather than making them yourself. On the other hand, you may be able to &quot;Analize&quot; natural phenomena, which I imagine Hypereconomics can't do<br /> <br /> Cybernetics ... maybe if you have installed the hardware that does that?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-22-2021, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T06:44:56-07:00","id":1445260,"title":"","content":"Clarifying this a bit, what Ramnesis is calling Analytics is an application of expertise as an instrument. You need to know the subject matter, usually represented as sufficient dots in an appropriate Ability \u2014 typically a Knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T07:47:05-07:00","id":1445264,"title":"","content":"Ehh...I can see that for &quot;detecting&quot;(making) a structural flaw on a building you would need to know architecture. But what's the expertice related with &quot;conveniently seeded technology&quot;?<br /> <br /> I would say *that* requires knowing that the Technocracy exists, that it does such things on occasion, knowing the secret to activate such devices, and having knowledge of what mundane corporations are under the umbrella of the Technocracy (to identify items that could be seeded)<br /> <br /> So...Hypertech? + a lot of Intel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T08:00:07-07:00","id":1445267,"title":"","content":"If you have <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/314476\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Made Easy</a>, check out the Tycoon Approach (pp.44\u201345). In particular: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For details about what this sorry of magick looks like in game terms, see <b>Mage 20</b>'s entries \u201cResources\u201d (pp.322\u2013323), \u201cFashion\u201d (p.591), \u201cMass Media\u201d, \u201cManagement and Human Resources\u201d, \u201cMoney and Wealth\u201d (pp.594\u2013596), and \u201cSocial Domination\u201d (p.598), plus the practice entries noted below and the character Malcolm Jamal Leonard (pp.254\u2013259).</div><br /> And<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Associated Practices:</b> Art of Desire/Hypereconomics, dominion, hypertech, invigoration, and reality-hacking.</div><br /> It also suggests that \u201ctycoon mages specialize in working with energy and influence (as described in the <b>How Do You DO That?</b> entries of those names, pp.42\u201351 and 114\u2013136).\u201d<br /> <br /> I would add that the \u201cworking with energy\u201d stuff is phrased in terms of \u201cworking with value\u201d. Resonance plays into this in that \u201cvalue\u201d isn't easily quantized; different Resonances represent different kinds of value. <br /> <br /> Conjuring material forms (HDYDT p.45) isn't done often by tycoons; when it is done, I'd have him practice hypertech through something like a 3d printer: the <b>Syndicate Convention Book</b> talks about them sometimes using hidden features of mundane technology; in this case, a 3d printer can make things that weren't there before, but a tycoon can use Primal Utility to enhance that beyond the strictly realistic limits of what a normal 3d printer can do. If he's willing to go Vulgar, he can enhance it <i>far</i> beyond its normal capabilities. In general, that's the Syndicate approach to hypertech: seemingly ordinary tech that has hidden features that make it inordinately effective. It generally doesn't add new capabilities, it just enhances existing features; and when it <i>does</i> add new features, they need to be logical extensions of the item's normal functions. The tycoon isn't going to find a gun hidden in a laptop, because guns aren't typically hidden in laptops. <br /> <br /> Another possibility is to use something akin to Dramatic Editing from <b>Adventure!</b>: if it's reasonable that a gun was just lying around and you simply haven't noticed it before now, then the tycoon could use expertise as an instrument to notice it. <br /> <br /> Conjuring immaterial forms (mind or spirit) pretty much <i>requires</i> hypertech; and since mundane tech that does something vaguely like this isn't exactly common (we don't exactly have holographic projectors yet), this is something that you're not going to see a tycoon doing; it falls the \u201cof you can't explain it within your Focus, you can't do it\u201d clause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T08:04:33-07:00","id":1445268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445264#post1445264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh...I can see that for &quot;detecting&quot;(making) a structural flaw on a building you would need to know architecture. But what's the expertice related with &quot;conveniently seeded technology&quot;?<br /> <br /> I would say *that* requires knowing that the Technocracy exists, that it does such things on occasion, knowing the secret to activate such devices, and having knowledge of what mundane corporations are under the umbrella of the Technocracy (to identify items that could be seeded)<br /> <br /> So...Hypertech? + a lot of Intel?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that they are aware that the Technocracy has seeded mundane technology so much as they are aware that there's more to what's in mundane technology that is normally known. I would use expertise in Technology for this purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T08:15:30-07:00","id":1445270,"title":"","content":"For the gun from laptop example, the Syndic might &quot;know&quot; that this certain model of laptop has a Iteration X alteration where the disc drive can be extracted via a secret command prompt and be able to be removed and &quot;fold&quot; into a gun.<br /> Probably definitely vulgar, but would fit as a Syndic as they are the marketers, they would know about &quot;premium&quot; Technocrat functions in Unenlightened technology.<br /> A stretch for sure, but might be enough to allow the Syndic access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T09:30:38-07:00","id":1445278,"title":"","content":"Maybe this is just me, and maybe the canon has lots of examples of Technocrats subconsciously reality-warping, but I see the Technocrats as probably being the least capable of getting away with these kind of post-hoc magical justifications; that secret door was &quot;always&quot; there, &quot;every&quot; new model of technology conveniently contains whatever hidden feature a nearby Technocrat needs. To the extent that their Paradigm/Focus strongly emphasizes rigidity and consistency, I think it's reasonable that the Technocracy needs to have more tangible limitations on what they can pull out of their @$$. Being able to fit a laser-gun inside of a laptop is Vulgar enough, I don't think they should be able to &quot;conveniently&quot; find one in any laptop laying around; they *should* have to find Technocrat brands that they know contain the appropriate features. I'm on the side of agreeing that sort of thing should be worked out with the ST when figuring out Focus during char-gen.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic paradigm comes with advantages; I lean somewhat towards the argument that the cheap mass-production of Devices and Wonders (lack of WP cost) that the Technocracy is capable of is an advantage that most Tradition Mages simply cannot replicate due to radical paradigm differences, for example.<br /> <br /> If a Technocrat is casting spontaneous Vulgar magic to the extent that they are just pulling junk out of nowhere without a strong rational justification in-paradigm, I'd imagine they'd be put on watch for signs of Reality Deviancy.<br /> <br /> PS It would probably require a lot of figuring-out between player and ST, but the name for such an Instrument would probably be &quot;Hidden Features,&quot; &quot;Executive Privilege,&quot; &quot;Developer Mode,&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:01:00-07:00","id":1445283,"title":"","content":"The \u201cgun in a laptop\u201d thing is something that I don't really condone; unless I missed something, Aleph brought it up as am example of how the notion of hidden features <i>shouldn't</i> be used; and I agree. <br /> <br /> But I absolutely <i>don't</i> agree that Technocrats are more \u201crigid\u201d than other mages; IMHO, that's a holdover from 1e when they were portrayed as agents of Stasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:10:32-07:00","id":1445287,"title":"","content":"I certainly don't mean it in the sense that they work towards something like the endgame of the Weaver. &quot;Pattern&quot; may have been a better word choice, reflecting something that can still be flexible and grow, but nonetheless is woven together and follows a consistent order. I don't think the statements &quot;Technocrats do not embody pure Stasis&quot; and &quot;Technocrats conform to a more rigid Paradigm than other Mages, even other Technomancers&quot; contradict one another.<br /> <br /> But I also haven't read Technocratic materials super deeply, I could still be overstating things.<br /> <br /> I think some people have been using the gun-in-a-laptop example as one they'd approve, but it's also why I included the mention of &quot;secrets doors that were conveniently always there&quot; that I recalled someone else mentioning. Apologies if I did misinterpret anyone's earlier posts.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think the most recent example is actually <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> with the idea of the &quot;convenient spy-bug on the fuse box those Reality Deviants are standing by.&quot; If the Technocrat knew that Technocratic groups had been involved in setting up the local power-grid, or there were signs that one had been custom modified by the Technocracy, for sure. But not just &quot;a fuse box? How CONVENIENT that our spy-bugs are always precisely where we need them to be!&quot; To contrast, I'm mostly down with the Analytics example, except I'm less for &quot;an obvious weakness that was not there before just is now because of Technocrat observation,&quot; but instead &quot;the Technocrat observer can detect a weakness that really isn't obvious, like the Peak Entropic State in the Quantum Harmonic Frequency of the structural beams, but it could still possibly pass as a 'lucky coincidence' to the HAP.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:11:22-07:00","id":1445298,"title":"","content":"Technocrats aren't primarily pattern either, they have all four of pattern, dynamic, primordial, and questing in their ranks.<br /> <br /> As well, they're not making something that wasn't there before suddenly appear. They're taking a situation that's ambiguous and removing the ambiguity. There might have been a secret panel there, or there might have been a bug. As long as it's plausible that those things might be, the Technocrat gets to say that they are.<br /> <br /> If you want some technobabble justification for this, I refer you to the wave function collapse in quantum mechanics. Prior to the collapse of the wave function, the state of reality is indeterminate. When the wave function is observed, it collapses to a definite state.<br /> <br /> But that's just one take on it. Most technocrats don't get into that sort of thing, and just describe it as \u201cI got lucky!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:21:19-07:00","id":1445299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1444956#post1444956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With PU 5 a Syndicate agent can bankrupt someone so hard, that someone will just cease to exist. That doesn't make sense?, well neither does erasing someone's &quot;code&quot; like if ppl were programs. Mages believe in weird shit.<br /> <br /> Even those not of the Syndicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one slipped by me during the first pass. I think I need to spend a lot more time learning about Primal Utility, but my gut reaction is Ugh. Virtual Adepts &quot;reality hacking&quot; doesn't bother me as much precisely because the Mercurial Elite have explicitly been described as embracing a more magical perspective AFAIK.<br /> <br /> And I'm not denying that the Technocracy includes more than just Pattern Essence Mages, just that they seem to make up an influential chunk. But maybe that is me projecting superficial interpretations from secondary sources too much, and I need to spend more time with the primary materials.<br /> <br /> I guess I just feel like Technocrats being able to get away with miraculous luck or &quot;science&quot; so soft that it needs to be kept in a jug takes away from the fun. That feels like what the Society of Ether is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:26:39-07:00","id":1445301,"title":"","content":"According to the upcoming Technocracy Reloaded, technocrats explicitly know that they are altering reality. They just do it in a scientific way rather than a magical way. I have my own pet theory on how that can be expressed in a way that isn't \u201ctechnocrats are liars and or dupes\u201d. If you want, I will give you a rundown of it. But it's important to keep in mind that Enlightened Science is every bit as dynamic as Magick is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:43:46-07:00","id":1445302,"title":"","content":"On my phone, so a bit brief.<br /> <br /> I don't take issue with Technocrats understanding that they are altering Reality. It's the details of how I'm getting a bit hung up on.<br /> <br /> Having your definition of &quot;science&quot; be loose enough that you can &quot;bankrupt people out of existence&quot; bothers me for a couple reasons: it seems to impair the ability of the Technocracy to be something close to a &quot;hard sci-fi&quot; faction, and it does make accepting the radical split tha Technocrats see between themselves and Mystics much harder.<br /> <br /> If the only difference between the acceptable way to warp Reality is whether you believe in God or Money, it just cheapens the conflict for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:02:16-07:00","id":1445305,"title":"","content":"The thing about the Technocracy is they are not really hung up on science as the correct way because it is science. They are hung up on science as the correct way because it is theirs. They have a specific way they want to take the world that will protect, control, and enlighten humanity (your mileage may vary on how much of each of those they are interested in) and technology is the way they think will do it the best.<br /> <br /> They didn't even start out naturalistic, that's just something that happened through internal political wrangling.<br /> <br /> Edit: What they believe in is a single paradigm world where people are unified, safe, and, depending on which Technocrat you talk to, free or safely under control. How they get there is more open than many of them would admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 04-22-2021, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:16:27-07:00","id":1445309,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I don't allow the Syndicate to \u201cbankrupt people out of existence\u201d \u2014 not because the Sphere doesn't allow it, but because the Focus doesn't allow it. If you're trying to use money as the instrument to cause something physical to disintegrate, it won't work. You'll need to use a different instrument for that sort of thing. Probably some sort of hypertech. Just like I've been pointing to 3D printers as the way to have something be created \u201cout of thin air\u201d. <br /> <br /> Just because the Sphere is called Primal Utility and was invented by the Syndicate, that doesn't mean that money is the proper Instrument to use for every Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:29:39-07:00","id":1445312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445309#post1445309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I don't allow the Syndicate to \u201cbankrupt people out of existence\u201d \u2014 not because the Sphere doesn't allow it, but because the Focus doesn't allow it. If you're trying to use money as the instrument to cause something physical to disintegrate, it won't work. You'll need to use a different instrument for that sort of thing. Probably some sort of hypertech. Just like I've been pointing to 3D printers as the way to have something be created \u201cout of thin air\u201d.<br /> <br /> Just because the Sphere is called Primal Utility and was invented by the Syndicate, that doesn't mean that money is the proper Instrument to use for every Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> here. I would allow a kind of induced Arcane where people and especially organizations have a hard time noticing a person because of their lack of resources, I would not allow actual physical dissolution. A Syndicate member could bankrupt you out of apparent existence, but not existence itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:37:01-07:00","id":1445313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445312#post1445312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> here. I would allow a kind of induced Arcane where people and especially organizations have a hard time noticing a person because of their lack of resources, I would not allow actual physical dissolution. A Syndicate member could bankrupt you out of apparent existence, but not existence itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, good, I am more in line with some folks than I feared, lol<br /> <br /> I myself was considering the very same thing about making you &quot;metaphorically&quot; disappear, but not &quot;physically&quot; disappear. You can use that Primal Energy to achieve that goal through some other form of Enlightened Science, but you can't just throw Money at something and make it explode because &quot;economics.&quot;<br /> <br /> PS That point above about the Technocracy wanting One Paradigm kind of hit on it, but I didn't know how to say it before, because even if it could fit the SYNDICATE Paradigm, it seems to contradict the wider TECHNOCRACY Paradigm, which requires stuff like Replicators, etc.<br /> <br /> Whereas I could imagine some Mystic burning a pile of money as a sacrifice in a ritual that could literally cause someone to vanish from existence. I can see that fitting into their Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-22-2021, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:57:25-07:00","id":1445319,"title":"","content":"To be frank I'm fine with the Syndicate being somewhat... odd, in comparism of everyone else. The Technocracy paradigm isn't a paradigm of science. It's a paradigm of slick, replicable laws in the universe that anyone with the right tools and knowledge can take advantage of. Iterators might get angry, but the NWO would probably nod along with the 'bankrupt someone to make someone cease to exist'. After all, they probably have an exact same rote that's like 1984.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:12:52-07:00","id":1445323,"title":"","content":"Kharnov: Yep. The issue is more of a mechanics thing than a concept thing, I think: specifically, The Syndicate convention book retooled Prime as Primal Utility because there were large chunks of it that could be reinterpreted in terms of value (e.g., sources of power and expenditures of Quintessence such as lowering difficulties or creating Wonders); but not everything could. This is one of those things that led me to develop a hack for the technocracy that rejiggers where the lines among the various Spheres lie. For example, I move a bunch of stuff that's in Primal Utility but can't be explained as value over to a slightly modified variant of Dimensional Science, which I call Void. The official products can't do that, though; data has to be able to do exactly the same things that correspondence can and vice versa, Primal utility has to be able to do exactly the same things that Prime can, and dimensional scientist has to be able to do exactly the same things that spirit can. You're allowed to make changes in terms of how well they can do things, such as how Primal utility gives easier access to the creation of Wonders but has more difficulty with physical manifestations; but changing which sphere gets used for a given effect would require tinkering with the entire set of spheres at once and can't be managed when you're addressing spheres one at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:18:23-07:00","id":1445326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445319#post1445319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank I'm fine with the Syndicate being somewhat... odd, in comparism of everyone else. The Technocracy paradigm isn't a paradigm of science. It's a paradigm of slick, replicable laws in the universe that anyone with the right tools and knowledge can take advantage of. Iterators might get angry, but the NWO would probably nod along with the 'bankrupt someone to make someone cease to exist'. After all, they probably have an exact same rote that's like 1984.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. 1984 didn't have people literally disappearing. I agree that the NWO and The Syndicate both have a wrote that lets them disappear someone; but in both cases, if they're doing it through propaganda / finances, it's a figurative disappearing, not a literal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:13:19-07:00","id":1445335,"title":"","content":"Putting my limited knowledge fully on display, the Wiki *does* describe limits to the Data Sphere that the Correspondence Sphere does not: requiring the presence of digital tech to function. Of course, I could imagine it fully supplanting Correspondence in the Digital Web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:26:25-07:00","id":1445337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445326#post1445326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. 1984 didn't have people literally disappearing. I agree that the NWO and The Syndicate both have a wrote that lets them disappear someone; but in both cases, if they're doing it through propaganda / finances, it's a figurative disappearing, not a literal one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, I'm ok with the upper ends of Enlightened Social Engineering or Hypereconomics blurring the lines into outright reality editing. They are aware of the Enlightened Anthropic Field (Consensus) as part of their more advanced scientific paradigm after all, so &quot;use propaganda to get the Enlightened Anthropic Field to expel this person from existence&quot; is something i'd allow as a practice for the appropriate, highly vulgar rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:30:28-07:00","id":1445357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445335#post1445335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting my limited knowledge fully on display, the Wiki *does* describe limits to the Data Sphere that the Correspondence Sphere does not: requiring the presence of digital tech to function. Of course, I could imagine it fully supplanting Correspondence in the Digital Web.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a limit in terms of what it can do. It's a limit in terms of how it can do it. That said, I find it a kind of odd limit; it's like building an instrument into the sphere. I have reworked that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T18:51:03-07:00","id":1448184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1445337#post1445337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm ok with the upper ends of Enlightened Social Engineering or Hypereconomics blurring the lines into outright reality editing. They are aware of the Enlightened Anthropic Field (Consensus) as part of their more advanced scientific paradigm after all, so &quot;use propaganda to get the Enlightened Anthropic Field to expel this person from existence&quot; is something i'd allow as a practice for the appropriate, highly vulgar rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> Technocrats are hardly without ways to BS truly extraordinary Effects. An NWO logician <i>literally</i> destroying a person with facts and logic is not impossible. It would just be Vulgar as hell, not to mention firmly against Union policy and more than a little uncouth. It also wouldn't be necessary, since the NWO agent has plenty of ways, in most situations, to figuratively destroy someone with facts and logic, or literally destroy them with some sort of solvent, flame-based weapon, or other material (not even getting into the still Vulgar high-tech disintegration rays).<br /> <br /> It's much the same with the Syndicate. Could a Syndicate rep bankrupt a person so hard that the invisible hand of the free market visibly unravels their existence? With enough time, a Syndicate rep could probably spin a BS explanation for why they can do it. The issue is that they wouldn't.<br /> <br /> I would totally believe, though, that a Syndicate rote could disrupt a person's capacity to obtain goods and services - metaphysically, disrupting their Pattern - to the extent that they cannot survive within the economy, and slowly waste away to nothing, even their corpse being repossessed by hobos and rats upon death until nothing of them remains.<br /> <br /> I mean, back in the Sorcerer's Crusade days, Order of Reason characters could use Correspondence to make overland travel quicker, or to infiltrate a buildings through lockpicks and climbing gear. Presumably they're using lesser forms of what the Spheres can do to accomplish their goals, just in a way that seems almost mundane (though if they were somehow studied with objective enough measures, someone after the fact would find their feat doesn't square with expectations). It makes sense, then, that Prime 5's ability to destroy someone could take the form of something happening so imperceptibly over time, it seemed like just a run of bad luck.<br /> <br /> Then again, if we're talking bad luck, the Syndicate rep could accomplish much the same financial ruination unto death using Entropy 5. Not merely using Entropy 4's ability to kill someone (just, you know, slowly), but to use Entropy 5 to make their existence have no value or presence within the minds of people around them. Such that they cannot hold down a job, have a bank account (the bank keeps wiping them from the system as a &quot;glitch&quot;), keep a home, or maintain interpersonal relationships. They slip from peoples' minds instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T19:46:27-07:00","id":1448189,"title":"","content":"Speaking to the topic and premises behind the topic, if you're looking for the Syndicate to expressly do things in &quot;mage X does Y thing, and due to a direct causal relationship between X and Y, Z occurs&quot; terms from a Doylist perspective, you're not getting very far. You're not getting very far with that perspective with <i>any</i> mage, tradition or technocrat. Let alone disparates, nephandi, or god help us, marauders.<br /> <br /> This is implicitly understood with tradition mages, because how else do we get rationale for hermetics slinging lightning bolts from the phallic symbol of that hermetic's choice? What the conversation's really about, is how does the Syndicate mage rationalize what they're doing, and how does that impact vulgarity.<br /> <br /> Now that I've gotten the statement of the obvious out of the way, why pick nits? And, why apply strict, restrictive language and conceptions of how mages do what they do?<br /> <br /> Creation <i>ex nihilo</i> doesn't necessarily <i>need</i> a Syndicate mage goofing off with a 3D printer, or some other convention's toys like some stupid Void Engineer's Star Trek fanboy replicator. They're the fucking Syndicate, they all but control global commerce. Hell, they're generally the Technocracy's requisitions department in all cases but convention-specific gear and requisite NWO oversight.<br /> <br /> All they need to do is file a requisition; the Primal Energy cost would be a deposit for the item or maybe some palm-greasing, a few phone calls or requested/called in favors would be the ritual roll. Goody arrives via courier or arrives at dead drop or in deposit/post box. If there's any organization on the planet that would have some deep web equivalent of Amazon -- or hell for that matter, a deep web-only extension of Amazon -- for buying the kinds of shit Syndicate mages would need, it's the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Where did the item come from? does it matter if it didn't actually exist before the Syndicate mage filed the requisition? who gives a shit! As long as the item doesn't just poof from existence in front of a sleeper, it isn't something truly ridiculous, or its inconvenient lack of existence can be reasonably explained away, it shouldn't be vulgar.<br /> <br /> How does this not get tracked by the NWO or Technocracy? Again, who gives a shit! NWO's smart but they're not omniscient. Who's to say some Syndicate associate or EC, or hell an algorithm for that matter, didn't receive the requisition and disappear it out of intra-convention loyalty or something. If there's any organization on the planet that would have some deeply-ingrained processes for off-record requisitions for agents, it's the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Hell the Syndicate probably <i>has</i> a fake requisitions officer whose entire non-existent job is the fulfillment of orders that didn't actually get placed, so that adequately-skilled agents can be told if they need to &quot;make a requisition&quot; they can file a request with Associate Akefay Ouchebag-Day, whose office is on the 13th Floor at 1060 W Addison St.<br /> <br /> From a Doylist perspective, is the Syndicate mage filing paperwork that doesn't matter, sending it to a requisitions office that doesn't exist, and in return some silly thing is poofing into existence at some random predetermined location? Well, <i>yeah</i>. But it's Mage, Mage doesn't work from a Doylist perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-10-2021, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T19:59:21-07:00","id":1448190,"title":"","content":"Just one nitpick: what you're describing isn't Vulgar. It's an example of a a Coincidental Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T20:54:44-07:00","id":1448194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448190#post1448190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one nitpick: what you're describing isn't Vulgar. It's an example of a a Coincidental Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's kind of my entire point. Look at the exchange on pages 1 and 2 about this very sub-topic, in which you were an active participant.<br /> <br /> People tend to get lost in the weeds talking about tools/foci and vulgarity versus being unable to rationalize an effect within a given paradigm, especially in terms of conceptualizing causality. That leads to people taking an approach that is much more constrictive than it needs to, or really should, be which with technocrats is only aggravated by how technocratic tools are discussed in published material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T03:09:59-07:00","id":1448207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448189#post1448189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking to the topic and premises behind the topic, if you're looking for the Syndicate to expressly do things in &quot;mage X does Y thing, and due to a direct causal relationship between X and Y, Z occurs&quot; terms from a Doylist perspective, you're not getting very far. You're not getting very far with that perspective with <i>any</i> mage, tradition or technocrat. Let alone disparates, nephandi, or god help us, marauders.<br /> <br /> This is implicitly understood with tradition mages, because how else do we get rationale for hermetics slinging lightning bolts from the phallic symbol of that hermetic's choice? What the conversation's really about, is how does the Syndicate mage rationalize what they're doing, and how does that impact vulgarity.<br /> <br /> Now that I've gotten the statement of the obvious out of the way, why pick nits? And, why apply strict, restrictive language and conceptions of how mages do what they do?<br /> <br /> Creation <i>ex nihilo</i> doesn't necessarily <i>need</i> a Syndicate mage goofing off with a 3D printer, or some other convention's toys like some stupid Void Engineer's Star Trek fanboy replicator. They're the fucking Syndicate, they all but control global commerce. Hell, they're generally the Technocracy's requisitions department in all cases but convention-specific gear and requisite NWO oversight.<br /> <br /> All they need to do is file a requisition; the Primal Energy cost would be a deposit for the item or maybe some palm-greasing, a few phone calls or requested/called in favors would be the ritual roll. Goody arrives via courier or arrives at dead drop or in deposit/post box. If there's any organization on the planet that would have some deep web equivalent of Amazon -- or hell for that matter, a deep web-only extension of Amazon -- for buying the kinds of shit Syndicate mages would need, it's the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Where did the item come from? does it matter if it didn't actually exist before the Syndicate mage filed the requisition? who gives a shit! As long as the item doesn't just poof from existence in front of a sleeper, it isn't something truly ridiculous, or its inconvenient lack of existence can be reasonably explained away, it shouldn't be vulgar.<br /> <br /> How does this not get tracked by the NWO or Technocracy? Again, who gives a shit! NWO's smart but they're not omniscient. Who's to say some Syndicate associate or EC, or hell an algorithm for that matter, didn't receive the requisition and disappear it out of intra-convention loyalty or something. If there's any organization on the planet that would have some deeply-ingrained processes for off-record requisitions for agents, it's the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Hell the Syndicate probably <i>has</i> a fake requisitions officer whose entire non-existent job is the fulfillment of orders that didn't actually get placed, so that adequately-skilled agents can be told if they need to &quot;make a requisition&quot; they can file a request with Associate Akefay Ouchebag-Day, whose office is on the 13th Floor at 1060 W Addison St.<br /> <br /> From a Doylist perspective, is the Syndicate mage filing paperwork that doesn't matter, sending it to a requisitions office that doesn't exist, and in return some silly thing is poofing into existence at some random predetermined location? Well, <i>yeah</i>. But it's Mage, Mage doesn't work from a Doylist perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I proposed this exact thing, more or less, on page 1 of this thread.<br /> <br /> Just as a person doesn't need &quot;chi points&quot; (from a biological or metaphysical perspective) for a martial artist to strike to block them and do an Effect, or a shaman doesn't need a fire spirit present for them to summon fire with Forces, so too does a Syndicate rep need an actual supply chain that a person could trace to have materials &quot;delivered&quot; to them. So long as the Syndicate rep believes such a supply chain exists - and that their actions tap that supply chain through their understanding of its nonexistent system - it will happen as they envision. That is, so long as they accrue enough successes on the casting. If they don't, then obviously the delivery got borked somewhere along the chain, and they need to send the order again. (And if they botch, well, there's always the chance you might have the wrong thing delivered, to inconvenient results).<br /> <br /> Trying to get too realistic or too meta with Mage is missing the point. You're playing a character who can make the impossible happen because they believed in it. It doesn't need to be reasonable. It just needs to be internally consistent within the character's Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T05:08:45-07:00","id":1448209,"title":"","content":"The thing is, this isn't a matter of Focus: M20 goes with &quot;Process Based Determinism&quot;. No taxis can appear to Corr 3 &quot;teleport&quot; Coincidentaly - if there aren't actual taxis, and/or you don't <i>make</i> them appear (which, in itself, could be Vulgar - and most likely require other Spheres).<br /> <br /> But I see how the Syndicate doesn't work under PBD. And so does the book, because the example they give it's not very PBD friendly - a helicopter sending the object you needed to you isn't different from teleport via taxi (just exchange the helicopter with a taxi, and the Prime materialized object example with a Correspondence summoned one)<br /> <br /> I can see why ppl would want to ignore that rule. BUT <i>this needs to be said</i>, if we all agree this is silly, let's drop it in it's entirety.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's fair to allow <i>only</i> the Syndicate to work w/o PBD. Plenty of magick could work that way, regardless of the Focus, if it was allowed - and this isn't obvious precisely because ppl assumes yoiu <i>have</i> to make the stuff appear in mid air with your Hermetic phalus, as if you had signed a contract to play with the D&amp;D spell list, instead of using the phalus to rework Reality(tm) to your advantage - you know, like mages do - to have the stuff <i>wrongly </i>delivered to you (still the same spell, if the end result it's what matters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-11-2021, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T07:25:53-07:00","id":1448214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448189#post1448189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking to the topic and premises behind the topic, if you're looking for the Syndicate to expressly do things in &quot;mage X does Y thing, and due to a direct causal relationship between X and Y, Z occurs&quot; terms from a Doylist perspective, you're not getting very far. You're not getting very far with that perspective with <i>any</i> mage, tradition or technocrat. Let alone disparates, nephandi, or god help us, marauders.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> From a Doylist perspective, is the Syndicate mage filing paperwork that doesn't matter, sending it to a requisitions office that doesn't exist, and in return some silly thing is poofing into existence at some random predetermined location? Well, <i>yeah</i>. But it's Mage, Mage doesn't work from a Doylist perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is broadly true, but it runs aground on the Syndicate Agent himself. He's going to need to know how the supply chain exists, how it works, and how it will manifest when it delivers. I think if we are at the point where the Syndicate has a fake department to mask that field agents aren't doing what they think they are doing then something has gone wrong. Nor do I think that problem goes away if said department or infrastructure doesn't exist but is just assumed.<br /> <br /> The Hermetic knows how his magic works and has spent quite a bit of time preparing his implements so they are ready to use when needed. His spell manifests the lightning, but it doesn't manifest the staff. That's already there. The supply network needs to be as well.<br /> <br /> That all being said. I think a Syndicate Agent would be very at home with the idea that there is much more connection between the numbers on the ledger and the actual shipping/recieving process than the typical sleeper thinks. Terms like Post Hoc Supply Chain Management and Just Before Time Inventory Systems come to mind. I could easily see him altering shipping routes and manifests so that an item which was in the warehouse was actually in a nearby truck. A kind of commerce based reality hacking.<br /> <br /> This is all, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, for a PBD system. If we are running Results Based Determinism things get much more fluid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T09:51:48-07:00","id":1448235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448214#post1448214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is broadly true, but it runs aground on the Syndicate Agent himself. He's going to need to know how the supply chain exists, how it works, and how it will manifest when it delivers. I think if we are at the point where the Syndicate has a fake department to mask that field agents aren't doing what they think they are doing then something has gone wrong. Nor do I think that problem goes away if said department or infrastructure doesn't exist but is just assumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mean first things first, doublethink and ignoring cognitive dissonance is kind of what the Technocracy does. That a Syndicate agent may be filing requisitions to a department they know doesn't actually exist, to justify acts like teleportation or creation ex nihilo, is totally fine when they're conditioned not to overthink it. What matters is they believe it works, and for them it would -- they're still mages however impenetrable their logic may be.<br /> <br /> This brings me back to my original point: <i>any</i> paradigm falls apart when put to the strain of undue scrutiny. The Syndicate isn't deserving of a higher degree of scrutiny than any other discrete group of mages.<br /> <br /> I ran into this issue in my most recent Technocrat game, in which someone who had only played TSC before decided to play a Syndicate agent and had a teeny bit of trouble wrapping her head around Ars Cupiditiae at first. Two-thirds of the people at my table are hardcore Trek fans, including her husband who's also one of my players, so the natural resolution to it was to direct her to the DS9 episode &quot;Treachery, Faith, and the Great River&quot;. What's relevant on the deeper level, is the Ferengi concept of the Great Material Continuum: their metaphysical principle that everything is connected via value, supply, and demand; that goods and services flow from supplier to demander in a way akin to the laws of thermodynamics; and, the nature of good business is to facilitate that flow from supplier to demander.<br /> <br /> That's Primal Utility in a nutshell, really.<br /> <br /> What's superficially relevant, is the character Nog launches on a series of trade deals, that involve some <i>extremely</i> odd items and shenanigans, leaving the audience to wonder how Nog knew the incredibly obscure set of info he knew, how the pieces all fit together, and how he managed to pull off some of the &quot;heists&quot; he did to facilitate the trade deals, in the first place. One could point at the episode and scream &quot;plot hole!&quot;...or they could not think about how Nog stole Sisko's desk without anyone noticing and enjoy the episode, and think &quot;how could I use this for inspiration for a Syndicate mage?&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is all, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, for a PBD system. If we are running Results Based Determinism things get much more fluid. </div> </div> </div>To a certain extent, this is the level of incrementalism I'm attacking. It's nice for discussing the game from a meta-narrative perspective, but highly dysfunctional when it comes to application in a game. That's actually why I dislike M20 to a certain extent, but particularly it's game supplements like HDYDT? which I personally straight-up reject at the table save sample rotes and examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T11:23:21-07:00","id":1448242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448235#post1448235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. I mean first things first, doublethink and ignoring cognitive dissonance is kind of what the Technocracy does. That a Syndicate agent may be filing requisitions to a department they know doesn't actually exist, to justify acts like teleportation or creation ex nihilo, is totally fine when they're conditioned not to overthink it. What matters is they believe it works, and for them it would -- they're still mages however impenetrable their logic may be.<br /> <br /> This brings me back to my original point: <i>any</i> paradigm falls apart when put to the strain of undue scrutiny. The Syndicate isn't deserving of a higher degree of scrutiny than any other discrete group of mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that in this case the Convention is propping up a paradigm it knows is a lie. It is deliberately building in an inconsistency that doesn't have to be there. It would be like the Akashics producing Wimp Lo <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kung Pow, Enter the Fist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Pay no attention to Wimp Lo, we purposely trained him wrong... as a joke&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it might technically work, but there's no upside to building a big weakness into your agents' world view. About the only scenario this might work for is captured and indoctrinated Reality Deviants.<br /> <br /> You are on much firmer ground with the Ferengi Metaphysics. We may not have a good understanding of how it works, but we can at least believe that the characters do. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a certain extent, this is the level of incrementalism I'm attacking. It's nice for discussing the game from a meta-narrative perspective, but highly dysfunctional when it comes to application in a game. That's actually why I dislike M20 to a certain extent, but particularly it's game supplements like HDYDT? which I personally straight-up reject at the table save sample rotes and examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>RBD and PBD are purely rules adjudication methods. They only take on any kind of meta-narrative quality if we selectively apply them to different paradigms. Some people do that, true, but I was not. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T12:55:50-07:00","id":1448255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448242#post1448242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RBD and PBD are purely rules adjudication methods. They only take on any kind of meta-narrative quality if we selectively apply them to different paradigms. Some people do that, true, but I was not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and neither am I.<br /> <br /> On the contrary, I strongly advocate against doing that. And I think this needs to be mentioned because it isn't <i>obvious</i> (non the least because the most recent edition it's taking a stance on RBD and PBD).<br /> <br /> It's easy to think the Syndicate it's having a <i>lesser </i>degree of scrutiny than Hermetics, when the Syndicate get's to teleport free of Paradox because reality just happens to provide them with a taxicab when they need to travel, while Hermetics have to eat 'dox to bend space OR need to explain where the taxi comes from (to determine the Spheres needed. And if it's going to be Vulgar, which would defeat the purpose).<br /> <br /> Taking a more general stance helps to clear this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-11-2021, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T15:06:17-07:00","id":1448262,"title":"","content":"Remember that M20 also uses the hypothetical average bystander. That means that you can summon an Uber (taxis are so last decade) without needing to know in advance whether there are any around. It's no different from pulling a coin out of your pocket: the HAB can't see into your pocket, and the HAB can't see what's around the block. So you don't <i>have</i> to determine whether or not an Uber actually <i>is</i> nearby before calling it; if you achieve the necessary successes in a \u201csummon a ride\u201d Effect, then there <i>is</i> one nearby. You didn't create it; it was already there. <br /> <br /> Note that this isn't a Syndicate vs. Hermetic thing: <i>both</i> can summon a ride from \u201coff-camera\u201d as a Coincidental Effect, differing only in the Practice and Instruments used to do the summoning. HAB allows that for everyone. In particular, Coincidence isn't about whether there's a rational connection between what the mage did and what followed; it's about whether what followed makes any sense on its own (though there <i>is</i> the Domino Effect to consider, for repeated Coincidences).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T05:09:59-07:00","id":1448312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448255#post1448255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easy to think the Syndicate it's having a <i>lesser </i>degree of scrutiny than Hermetics, when the Syndicate get's to teleport free of Paradox because reality just happens to provide them with a taxicab when they need to travel, while Hermetics have to eat 'dox to bend space OR need to explain where the taxi comes from (to determine the Spheres needed. And if it's going to be Vulgar, which would defeat the purpose).<br /> <br /> Taking a more general stance helps to clear this out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If something such as a full taxicab is a bit much for reality to provide free of charge (on the grounds that it breaks my suspension of disbelief) it must be accounted for no matter who is casting. Something small enough to come &quot;free of charge&quot; (a door that wasn't there before and isn't the next time you look works for me, but may be a bridge too far for others) it is &quot;free of charge&quot; for everyone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T05:57:13-07:00","id":1448316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448312#post1448312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. If something such as a full taxicab is a bit much for reality to provide free of charge (on the grounds that it breaks my suspension of disbelief) it must be accounted for no matter who is casting. Something small enough to come &quot;free of charge&quot; (a door that wasn't there before and isn't the next time you look works for me, but may be a bridge too far for others) it is &quot;free of charge&quot; for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why does the ride break your suspension of disbelief? How do you know that it <i>wasn't</i> already there, just offstage, right before your mage summoned it? Everyone seems to be assuming that it wasn't; but why make that assumption?<br /> <br /> That's the whole <i>point</i> of Coincidental Magick: it's stuff that <i>might have happened anyway</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-12-2021, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T07:05:59-07:00","id":1448320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448316#post1448316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why does the ride break your suspension of disbelief? How do you know that it <i>wasn't</i> already there, just offstage, right before your mage summoned it? Everyone seems to be assuming that it wasn't; but why make that assumption?<br /> <br /> That's the whole <i>point</i> of Coincidental Magick: it's stuff that <i>might have happened anyway</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not assuming that at all. If the spell just summons a cab that is never a problem because the cab is the purpose of the spell. It is accounted for by definition. If the spell uses a cab as a mechanism for something else and then doesn't account for the cab that starts pushing on my disbelief. Going back to previous examples, a spell that causes a convenient item to be delivered by UPS can't just be a teleportation of the convenient item (in PBD), it also has to account for the truck and driver, even if that is as simple as bringing in an assumed truck from around the corner.<br /> <br /> This is not something I try to get into the weeds on. A lot of spells have extraneous elements that don't really need explanations. The truck changes too much about the scene to ignore, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T07:17:05-07:00","id":1448321,"title":"","content":"Does it, though? You work your Magick; a UPS truck pulls up, the driver hands you a package and asks you to sign for it, and then drives off. What's changed about the scene, other than you now having the package? <br /> <br /> I'll grant that if the service is implausibly fast, that could be a problem; UPS delivers days later, not seconds. But other than that, what's the problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T08:08:32-07:00","id":1448323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448321#post1448321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it, though? You work your Magick; a UPS truck pulls up, the driver hands you a package and asks you to sign for it, and then drives off. What's changed about the scene, other than you now having the package?<br /> <br /> I'll grant that if the service is implausibly fast, that could be a problem; UPS delivers days later, not seconds. But other than that, what's the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That depends a great deal on the pacing of the scene. If it is just happening during the course of an average day, not much. If it is happening during something tense like a manhunt or a chase, quite a bit. It's not how the scene is changed after the truck leaves, it is how much it is changed during the time the truck is there.<br /> <br /> Edit: And no, I am not suggesting that the sphere requirements of a spell should depend on whether the mood is tense or relaxed. Instead I am saying that the truck changes enough in enough situations that I have a hard time thinking of it as window dressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-12-2021, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T08:29:22-07:00","id":1448324,"title":"","content":"So it isn't the vehicle that the issue per se, it's the context. Fair enough. Coincidence has always been very dependent on context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T09:55:59-07:00","id":1448329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448324#post1448324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it isn't the vehicle that the issue per se, it's the context. Fair enough. Coincidence has always been very dependent on context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Coincidentialiy is not my issue. I have no problem with assuming a nearby UPS truck or any other reasonably plausible thing about the world. That's not even a Mage thing, it is my standard stance for any RPG. However, I would not assume the truck just interjects itself at a convenient moment without help. <br /> <br /> Thus in PBD, bringing that truck from wherever it is to the mage is a part of the spell and must be accounted for in the sphere cost. I wouldn't impose this for a largely cosmetic issue but the truck has a narrative weight and an effect on the flow of the game while it is present. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T10:23:41-07:00","id":1448331,"title":"","content":"I guess I just don't assign the same narrative weight to it that you do. For me it's as I said before: you do your thing, the truck arrives, hands off the package, and drives off. I find that no different than conveniently finding a knife lying around. Context permitting, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-12-2021, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T10:37:47-07:00","id":1448332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448242#post1448242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that in this case the Convention is propping up a paradigm it knows is a lie. It is deliberately building in an inconsistency that doesn't have to be there...</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's a lie but it works, then it wasn't a lie. <i>All</i> paradigms are lies, and <i>all</i> groups of mages engage in doublethink and prop up lies whether they explicitly acknowledge it or not. That's no more obvious in practice than mystics eschewing tools and foci as they grow more powerful, and come to the understanding paradigm isn't what makes their shit work in the first place. They do it because it's easier to externalize belief, even though that externalized belief is completely illusory.<br /> <br /> Technocrats just happen to be mages who specialize in doublethink, to make their shit simpler and standardized. And the &quot;doublethink&quot; of this is the key, simply for how technocrats deliberately overlook the complete lack of logical consistency of their own work, on the micro scale, in order to ensure it works on the macro scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RBD and PBD are purely rules adjudication methods. They only take on any kind of meta-narrative quality if we selectively apply them to different paradigms. Some people do that, true, but I was not. </div> </div> </div>They're inherently metanarrative; Mage is a game <i>about</i> metanarrative and metanarrative cannot be divorced from any of its concepts how strongly divorced from the setting, metaplot, or even mechanics, it may seem on first glance. Mage PC's are, in effect, ST's from a Watsonian perspective; the rules you're attempting to adjudicate are how characters act as the editorial board for their own personal, and interconnected, narratives in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'll put it another way: fuck &quot;PBD&quot;, fuck &quot;RBD&quot;, fuck &quot;HAB&quot;, fuck &quot;HOO&quot;. Imagine that instead of interactive storytelling, your average game of Mage was a television show or movie, and we're going with &quot;Hopeless Average Viewer&quot; (HAV) and &quot;Habitual Asshole Neckbeard&quot; (HAN). Anything that happens that'll cause HAN to run to their computer and make a 10:06-long YouTube ragebait video for dat ad revenue about how Mage: the Televisioning was full of plot holes and totally unwatchable, well that's just magic. Something that happens that's blatant enough to cause HAV to put down their popcorn and say, &quot;huh?&quot; is <i>vulgar</i> magic.<br /> <br /> HAV checks out and barely pays any attention to what's going on screen at all, and doesn't really think about it too hard. So if a character pulls a gun out of a pocket in a scene when the film/movie didn't establish they had one in their pocket to begin with, they're not going to notice or care. HAN is a nitpicking shithead that doesn't really care about the circumstances or context of the scene, they just get pissy because there wasn't an establishing shot of the person having a gun in their pocket.<br /> <br /> You're probably wondering right now what the effective difference between what I'm suggesting is between HAB and HOO. There isn't any, because it was about metanarrative in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T10:47:22-07:00","id":1448333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448331#post1448331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just don't assign the same narrative weight to it that you do. For me it's as I said before: you do your thing, the truck arrives, hands off the package, and drives off. I find that no different than conveniently finding a knife lying around. Context permitting, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I keep defaulting to this happening in the middle of a firefight, so the truck has (potentially) a bigger effect on the action than the spell it is facilitating. It wouldn't have that big an effect on a relaxed, sunny afternoon, but I don't want to change the sphere cost due to context. If I have to choose between counting bringing the truck as part of the process or ignoring that aspect, I'm going to count it as part of the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T10:49:13-07:00","id":1448334,"title":"","content":"And remember, HAN gets shot first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:01:04-07:00","id":1448335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448262#post1448262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that M20 also uses the hypothetical average bystander. That means that you can summon an Uber (taxis are so last decade) without needing to know in advance whether there are any around. It's no different from pulling a coin out of your pocket: the HAB can't see into your pocket, and the HAB can't see what's around the block. So you don't <i>have</i> to determine whether or not an Uber actually <i>is</i> nearby before calling it; if you achieve the necessary successes in a \u201csummon a ride\u201d Effect, then there <i>is</i> one nearby. You didn't create it; it was already there.<br /> <br /> Note that this isn't a Syndicate vs. Hermetic thing: <i>both</i> can summon a ride from \u201coff-camera\u201d as a Coincidental Effect, differing only in the Practice and Instruments used to do the summoning. HAB allows that for everyone. In particular, Coincidence isn't about whether there's a rational connection between what the mage did and what followed; it's about whether what followed makes any sense on its own (though there <i>is</i> the Domino Effect to consider, for repeated Coincidences).</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it can be (and it's intended to be) Coincidental its part of the issue.'And part of why I think it's important to clarify this point about PBD.<br /> <br /> The <i>process </i>of materializing a car with a person, and stuff costs more (in terms of Spheres and successes) than regular teleportation (Corr 3 vs. whatever you need to make a taxi - I.E: it's Corr 4, if you're teleporting it from somewhere else. Prime 2 + Matter and Life to materialize the taxi and the driver... etc. ).<br /> The difference between PBD and RBD it's <i>greater</i> in HAP, because the latter has an easier time constructing Coincidental Effects precisely for the reasons you mention (albeit I'm not sure if a &quot;corner&quot; of a street, that may be heavily populated with NPC looking at that corner, driving trough there, etc...can be realy compared with a pocket - but that's a different matter).<br /> <br /> Hence why I stress so much this PBD thing. What changes here isn't Coincidence, but rather the Spheres and successes needed to cast an Effect (in a Coincidental way).<br /> <br /> Or in other words, the kind of <i>bullshit</i> a player it's expected to try in the game (and how).<br /> <br /> I need to know, as a player, that these things are viable ways to gain the advantages of Coincidence, and M20 certainly doesn't point me towards that with that PBD section. <i>Less so </i>because it's HAP - hence I think it matters to say: &quot;Yeah, I don't quite agree with M20 stance here&quot;. That way I'm not going to think I can't do the taxicab teleport just because I lack the Spheres to summon an actual, <i>meaningful</i>, taxi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-12-2021, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:04:25-07:00","id":1448336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448333#post1448333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair enough. I keep defaulting to this happening in the middle of a firefight, so the truck has (potentially) a bigger effect on the action than the spell it is facilitating. It wouldn't have that big an effect on a relaxed, sunny afternoon, but I don't want to change the sphere cost due to context. If I have to choose between counting bringing the truck as part of the process or ignoring that aspect, I'm going to count it as part of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, this is where it being coincidental comes into play: a Syndic isn't even going to bother to try to summon the truck if it can't be done coincidentally. Which means that he's not going to do it in the middle of a firefight, or at any other time when the context would be wrong. So you don't need to worry about the potential problems of calling a truck into the middle of a firefight, because it's not gonna happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:16:29-07:00","id":1448337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448332#post1448332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a lie but it works, then it wasn't a lie. <i>All</i> paradigms are lies, and <i>all</i> groups of mages engage in doublethink and prop up lies whether they explicitly acknowledge it or not. That's no more obvious in practice than mystics eschewing tools and foci as they grow more powerful, and come to the understanding paradigm isn't what makes their shit work in the first place. They do it because it's easier to externalize belief, even though that externalized belief is completely illusory.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not have the same view of Mage at all and I'm not even sure how to translate back and forth in this case. I don't consider paradigms to be lies. I assume they are internally consistent even if I don't know the details. I also don't think mages drop paradigms when they drop instruments.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that last one is M20s stance on dropping instruments too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448332#post1448332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HAV checks out and barely pays any attention to what's going on screen at all, and doesn't really think about it too hard. So if a character pulls a gun out of a pocket in a scene when the film/movie didn't establish they had one in their pocket to begin with, they're not going to notice or care. HAN is a nitpicking shithead that doesn't really care about the circumstances or context of the scene, they just get pissy because there wasn't an establishing shot of the person having a gun in their pocket.<br /> <br /> You're probably wondering right now what the effective difference between what I'm suggesting is between HAB and HOO. There isn't any, because it was about metanarrative in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Nasally voice* Well technically the HAN is just an annoyingly perceptive HAB. He can't be a HOO because he can't see inside pockets unless the camera is there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:26:03-07:00","id":1448339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448336#post1448336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, this is where it being coincidental comes into play: a Syndic isn't even going to bother to try to summon the truck if it can't be done coincidentally. Which means that he's not going to do it in the middle of a firefight, or at any other time when the context would be wrong. So you don't need to worry about the potential problems of calling a truck into the middle of a firefight, because it's not gonna happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to solve a problem, I'm trying to explain why I think truck summoning is significant enough to be considered part of the process.<br /> <br /> Also, who is to say this will always be done by a Syndicate Agent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:41:21-07:00","id":1448341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448337#post1448337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We do not have the same view of Mage at all and I'm not even sure how to translate back and forth in this case. I don't consider paradigms to be lies. I assume they are internally consistent even if I don't know the details. I also don't think mages drop paradigms when they drop instruments.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that last one is M20s stance on dropping instruments too.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, you're right about this: the notion that you drop paradigm as your Arete increases was itself dropped in M20: in M20, your Paradigms and Practices never go away; and the removal of Instruments in non-Technocrat Foci as Arete increases is more a matter of realizing that they're not <i>strictly</i> necessary to implement the Practice. <br /> <br /> (That said, I find the way this is implemented in M20 to be kind of clunky, and house-rule it to be a matter of whether your source of power is internal or external rather than mystical or technomantic; and with external sources resulting in Instruments that never go away but which ultimately have greater aptitude with their use, while internal sources let you Work Without Focus and surpass your Instruments as your Arete increases, but has less altitude with Instruments than external sources have.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T12:12:15-07:00","id":1448345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448339#post1448339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to solve a problem, I'm trying to explain why I think truck summoning is significant enough to be considered part of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I treat it as part of the Instruments: Management and Human Resources. You're getting an existing delivery network to do your bidding, and then empowering it to accomplish the task more efficiently than they normally would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T22:20:04-07:00","id":1448391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448345#post1448345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I treat it as part of the Instruments: Management and Human Resources. You're getting an existing delivery network to do your bidding, and then empowering it to accomplish the task more efficiently than they normally would.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> The truck doesn't need to spontaneously pop into existence for the Effect to work. It just needs to be a vector for the actual Effect to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T05:28:29-07:00","id":1448409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448345#post1448345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I treat it as part of the Instruments: Management and Human Resources. You're getting an existing delivery network to do your bidding, and then empowering it to accomplish the task more efficiently than they normally would.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Treating it as an instrument and using an associated skill check is certainly a way of accounting for the truck. The skill check is listed as optional, I think, but I'm an advocate of using mundane skills to ground the magic in the world. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T05:41:27-07:00","id":1448410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448345#post1448345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I treat it as part of the Instruments: Management and Human Resources. You're getting an existing delivery network to do your bidding, and then empowering it to accomplish the task more efficiently than they normally would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Empowering an existing delivery network to do your bidding it's significantly different from summoning an object, though.<br /> <br /> Let's say my Instrument it's a magick wand. Can I use Prime 2 + Matter 3 to empower an existing delivery network that I know off, because I have relevant Skills/Backgrounds, into materilizing an object for me?, or only the ones that use the same instruments/practice as the Syndicate get to do that with Spheres that can't normaly teleport trucks nor empower any kind of network into doing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T06:41:44-07:00","id":1448415,"title":"","content":"I have never suggested teleporting trucks. Not once have I ever said anything about a truck suddenly being there when it hadn't been before. What I have suggested is saying that a truck that <i>might</i> have been there now <i>definitely is</i> there. That's why I brought up HAB. <br /> <br /> As for \u201cempowering an existing network\u201d, that's not an Effect; that's a summary of the description of the Management and Human Resources box. So no, if you're not using Management and Human Resources, then obviously you're not going to \u201cempower an existing network to function more efficiently\u201d; that would be like asking if you get to stab someone without using a sharp object: using a sharp object is what makes it \u201cstabbing\u201d. \u201cEmpowering a service\u201d isn't an <i>Effect</i>; it's <i>how the Effect manifests through the (Management and Human Resources) Instrument</i>. The <i>Effect</i> is that you get your package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-13-2021, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T07:11:02-07:00","id":1448417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448415#post1448415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never suggested teleporting trucks. Not once have I ever said anything about a truck suddenly being there when it hadn't been before. What I have suggested is saying that a truck that <i>might</i> have been there now <i>definitely is</i> there. That's why I brought up HAB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to repeat myself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The difference between PBD and RBD it's <i>greater</i> in HAP</b>, because the latter has an easier time constructing Coincidental Effects precisely for the reasons you mention</div> </div> </div> </div>How in the name of heaven does the HAP (a tool to diferentiate between Vulgar and Coindcidental) causes a <i>convinient </i>truck that <i>might</i> have been there <i>definitely </i>be there -<b><i>always </i></b>- when you cast an effect that needs it to be there?<br /> <br /> What you propose it's on the level of Exalted Charms that alter the narrative to benefit the Exalt. &quot;There's always a truck when you need to materialize something, so it isn't going to be Vulgar - ever&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for \u201cempowering an existing network\u201d, that's not an Effect; that's a summary of the description of the Management and Human Resources box. So no, if you're not using Management and Human Resources, then obviously you're not going to \u201cempower an existing network to function more efficiently\u201d; that would be like asking if you get to stab someone without using a sharp object: using a sharp object is what makes it \u201cstabbing\u201d. \u201cEmpowering a service\u201d isn't an <i>Effect</i>; it's <i>how the Effect manifests through the (Management and Human Resources) Instrument</i>. The <i>Effect</i> is that you get your package. </div> </div> </div>*Shooting as an Instrument doesn't give you infinte ammo if you don't cast a spell to give your gun infinitte ammo.<br /> *Using moon phases as instrument doesn't include the moon being in the phase you need to cast a spell all the time.<br /> *And a spell that summons a package doesn't include the convencience of a whole truck that migth be there <i>definitely </i>being there to mask your summoning of something much smaller, unless you actually cast a spell to transform that &quot;migth&quot; into a fact (Entropy comes to mind, if it's really plausible - which actually isn't, you're transforming a <i>minuscule </i>probability into a certain fact<i>. </i>For free, using your ST fiat) to assist him<br /> <br /> The effect includes a fucking truck that's appearing whenever you want, to mask it as a Coincidence. You're allowing the Syndicate a level of narrative <i>power no other instrument has. This is exactly what I mean when I say that the Syndicate it's being scrutinized LESS than any other mage in the setting. </i><br /> <br /> Oh, and spirits <i>don't</i> just appear whenever a Dreamspeaker wants to cast a fireball. Not w/o Spirit. Not under PBD. \u00b4This has been a long lasting topic with the Tradition (why do they believe they're summning spirits, when anyone can see summoning a spirit requires Spirit? - The answers are either screw PBD, or manage to spin it in a way you don't require the pressence of actual Umbroods to cast an effect. Or, well, make sure to have the rigth spirits arround you).<br /> <br /> So I don't buy the crap of &quot;Mystic paradigms are being less scrutinized&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T07:27:48-07:00","id":1448418,"title":"","content":"Technocracy paradigm has always been a bit funny for me because the books are so inconsistent. Alot of the time its &quot;this involves machines so they can do it&quot; without really saying how they think they can do it. The example rote in the Technocracy reloaded with all the guns is a good example. Exactly what does the technocrat think they are doing.<br /> I'd like to see a canon example of a technocrats paradigm, along with a bunch of adjustments and procedures they use and the thinking behind them. Hell I'd love to see this for a whole bunch of factions.<br /> <br /> I'd start with some premises.<br /> 1. Technocrats understand their own workings as enlightened science<br /> 2. Technocrats understand that they are making something happened themselves<br /> 3. technocrats believe in their own paradigm<br /> <br /> This immediately removes things like opening a cupboard to find just the materials you needed with a matter adjustment. What exactly would the technocrat understand to be happening there? Theres no science, no understanding. Thats magic working subconciously and mystically. No, instead a technocrat would be able to utilise the properties of the matter around him, properties only understandable through enlightened science, to do what he wants. He might need some device or tool, but making a chair, a phone and three yards of curtain into an explosive should be entirely possible once he has used his gluon blending ray device (GBRD) to excite the chair molecules in exactly the right way. And yeah thats vulgar.<br /> <br /> It also removes things like using a rote to give a car a plasma blaster. Either the car had it originally, in which case its a wonder, or it didn't. How would a technocrat understand getting into someones honda civic and activating a plasma blaster? Maybe if they had time to work on it for a bit they could build a plasma blaster. But not as a rote cast in the middle of a hot pursuit.<br /> <br /> Technocratic should have no aspect of luck, chance or &quot;it was there all along&quot;.<br /> What it should have is lots of wonders, lots of subtle adjustments using understanding to exploit hidden properties of things, and lots of using covert scientific/engineering apparatus. Use your VDAS and some custom software to scan that building for weak spots, but don't just happen to find them.<br /> <br /> As for the syndicate agent flatlining someones worth so badly they cease to exist. This is ENTIRELY possible, but its not prime, its entropy and prime. The syndicate agent bankrupts them, fires them, just generally flatlines everything about their value and then lets fate take the wheel. The poor target, homeless, friendless, jobless, then meets their end in some sad fashion. Maybe they take an overdose, maybe they die of grief, maybe they take their own life. Maybe they live but just cease to be relevant to power and worth. Maybe they become a permanent member of the homeless population, maybe they just wander off and are never heard from again. To the syndicate agent, they have been destroyed, the details aren't important. Note that I think this is only really possible with entropy which explicitly allows some form of flexibility between intention and outcome. But entropy seems like such a key sphere for syndicate workings.<br /> <br /> As to the original post, how does a syndicate agent make a knife do agg damage. In my playing of the syndicate, he doesn't. Thats not really something that they do. He might have a trinket knife that he paid a massive amount of money for, that does agg damage. And it might do agg damage because he paid a massive amount of money for it, so its primal utility is invested into it through the sheer cost. But I don't see syndicate agents doing this on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T09:08:12-07:00","id":1448428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448417#post1448417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Allow me to repeat myself:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How in the name of heaven does the HAP (a tool to diferentiate between Vulgar and Coindcidental) causes a <i>convinient </i>truck that <i>might</i> have been there <i>definitely </i>be there -<b><i>always </i></b>- when you cast an effect that needs it to be there?<br /> <br /> What you propose it's on the level of Exalted Charms that alter the narrative to benefit the Exalt. &quot;There's always a truck when you need to materialize something, so it isn't going to be Vulgar - ever&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Shooting as an Instrument doesn't give you infinte ammo if you don't cast a spell to give your gun infinitte ammo.<br /> *Using moon phases as instrument doesn't include the moon being in the phase you need to cast a spell all the time.<br /> *And a spell that summons a package doesn't include the convencience of a whole truck that migth be there <i>definitely </i>being there to mask your summoning of something much smaller, unless you actually cast a spell to transform that &quot;migth&quot; into a fact (Entropy comes to mind, if it's really plausible - which actually isn't, you're transforming a <i>minuscule </i>probability into a certain fact<i>. </i>For free, using your ST fiat) to assist him<br /> <br /> The effect includes a fucking truck that's appearing whenever you want, to mask it as a Coincidence. You're allowing the Syndicate a level of narrative <i>power no other instrument has. This is exactly what I mean when I say that the Syndicate it's being scrutinized LESS than any other mage in the setting. </i><br /> <br /> Oh, and spirits <i>don't</i> just appear whenever a Dreamspeaker wants to cast a fireball. Not w/o Spirit. Not under PBD. \u00b4This has been a long lasting topic with the Tradition (why do they believe they're summning spirits, when anyone can see summoning a spirit requires Spirit? - The answers are either screw PBD, or manage to spin it in a way you don't require the pressence of actual Umbroods to cast an effect. Or, well, make sure to have the rigth spirits arround you).<br /> <br /> So I don't buy the crap of &quot;Mystic paradigms are being less scrutinized&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the truck isn't the instrument; the delivery service is. What the syndic needs in order to be able to work the Effect is access to the service.<br /> <br /> Second, the truck is only certain to be there when the Effect succeeds. And with the Domino Effect, attempting to spam it makes it increasingly likely that the Effect will fail. So no, the truck isn't there all the time.<br /> <br /> And third: no, I'm not transforming the miniscule probability into a certainty. That's what I was talking to Ramnesis about<b></b>: context matters. This actually is very similar to your spirits example: you're not going to be able to get a UPS truck show up and hand you a package if you're in the middle of the wilderness, for example. It needs to be a time and place where it would be plausible that a delivery truck might be there. Just like you need the right spirits to be present if you're concept of your Magick is that it's all spirit-assisted. <br /> <br /> Where I'm coming from with this is that in many cases, Coincidental Magick is to Mage as Dramatic Editing is to the Trinity Continuum or Twists of Fate are to Scion. In each of these cases, the reality that you're dealing with is more cinematic than realistic. You can see this in M20, where the Technocracy's counterpart to mythic threads are the hypernarratives: basically, if it's a \u201cmovie reality\u201d thing, them you get -1 Difficulty on your working for tapping into a hypernarrative. Coincidental Effects that actually represent the kinds of coincidences that make up such a big part of cinematic reality are part and parcel to this. <br /> <br /> And you keep reading \u201cmight have been\u201d as \u201cwasn't, until the mage changed things\u201d. That's specifically <i>not</i> what I'm talking about. The Storyteller can't be expected to pre-establish every detail about the scene and the surrounding environment; so a lot of details (such as whether or not there are any delivery trucks nearby) <i>aren't known by anyone</i>, because the Storyteller didn't nail them down. And <i>that's</i> where the convenient delivery truck resides: in those details that haven't been specified. That's why I brought up HAB vs. HOO: the latter assumes that every detail has been nailed down; the former doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T10:14:52-07:00","id":1448434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the truck isn't the instrument; the delivery service is. What the syndic needs in order to be able to work the Effect is access to the service.</div> </div> </div> </div>The truck it's part of the delivery service. But , of course, the agent doesn't need the truck to be there - a phonecall it's enough. What's suspicious it's that the magick <i>includes </i>the truck being there<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, the truck is only certain to be there when the Effect succeeds. And with the Domino Effect, attempting to spam it makes it increasingly likely that the Effect will fail. So no, the truck isn't there all the time. </div> </div> </div>And thus it's part of the effect...<br /> <br /> Can't you see how ludicrous it is to say that an Arete rol determines the &quot;chance&quot; of a truck being there...yet isnsisting that summoning a truck isn't part of the Effect?<br /> <br /> Let's say I want a truck, but I don't have the Spheres/successes to call one fast enough. Yet I have the Spheres/successes to materialize a smaller, less complex, item. So, knowing how you rol, I summon an item to be delivered via truck - almost instantly, of course.<br /> <br /> Then proceed to take control of the truck, and throw the item out of the window. I just wanted the truck to come fast enough, after all. How can you still spin I <i>didn't</i> just summoned a truck, if that happens?<br /> <br /> And, yeah, I know, that will have &quot;consequences&quot; (of an angry ST) - that's not the point here. The point it's that the free serendipity summoning it's very real, and how that goes against PBD<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And third: no, I'm not transforming the miniscule probability into a certainty. That's what I was talking to Ramnesis about<b></b>: context matters. This actually is very similar to your spirits example: you're not going to be able to get a UPS truck show up and hand you a package if you're in the middle of the wilderness, for example. It needs to be a time and place where it would be plausible that a delivery truck might be there. Just like you need the right spirits to be present if you're concept of your Magick is that it's all spirit-assisted. </div> </div> </div>HOW plausible<br /> <br /> Because the way you seem to roll, the truck it's appearing ungodly fast, in a place where using mundane means it would take longer. You're making examples that make me question if it's realy plausible<br /> <br /> it seems that &quot;being in a city&quot; it's plausible enough for you. it is not plausible enough for me. Because the truck appears faster than it normaly would, and appears only if you're using magick that needs it to appear, then <i>I fail to not see it as part of the effect</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where I'm coming from with this is that in many cases, Coincidental Magick is to Mage as Dramatic Editing is to the Trinity Continuum or Twists of Fate are to Scion. In each of these cases, the reality that you're dealing with is more cinematic than realistic. You can see this in M20, where the Technocracy's counterpart to mythic threads are the hypernarratives: basically, if it's a \u201cmovie reality\u201d thing, them you get -1 Difficulty on your working for tapping into a hypernarrative. Coincidental Effects that actually represent the kinds of coincidences that make up such a big part of cinematic reality are part and parcel to this. </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the effect isn't going to be Coincidental - that's a different debate. I'm saying the Effect includes a truck w/o the Spheres needed to include a truck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you keep reading \u201cmight have been\u201d as \u201cwasn't, until the mage changed things\u201d. That's specifically <i>not</i> what I'm talking about. The Storyteller can't be expected to pre-establish every detail about the scene and the surrounding environment; so a lot of details (such as whether or not there are any delivery trucks nearby) <i>aren't known by anyone</i>, because the Storyteller didn't nail them down. And <i>that's</i> where the convenient delivery truck resides: in those details that haven't been specified. </div> </div> </div>That is <b>the very definition of Storyteller's Fiat</b><br /> <br /> I'm 100% ok with a player asking if there's one truck nearby, and the ST either saying yes or no depending on what's best for the plot, or even rolling a dice if the ST does not know.<br /> I'm 100% against using this fiat to make coicidences easier for the Syndicate, and call it the way their magick works. Unless you allow everyone to benefit from the same coincidences - and you're not doing that in your examples.<br /> <br /> You're using ST fiat to provide free serendipity, but only for Technocrats. The fact that you're not doing the same for the Dreamspeaker in the example above it's <i>outrageous </i>(what?, there couldn't be a fire spirit in the Penumbra whenever I call it with my totem?). It really talks spades about <i>whom </i>it's receiving more scrutiny here, if the shaman needs to <i>actually </i>call a spirit with magick, but the Syndic doesn't need to deal with any bureaucracy nor with the speed of transport.<br /> <br /> The thing is: If you need to succeed at an Arete roll for it to happen, then it wasn't there. If it's magick, then it wasn't there. The characters may not know this chain of events happened, but you and I do.<br /> <br /> Why it's a truck there when the Syndicate calls, but not when any other does? <i>It's because it's part of the magick. </i><br /> <br /> Too bad only Human Resources can have their mojo working that way. It seems that you can't simply Prime 2/Matter an object via truck trough communing with the spirit of comerce and resources with your totem - that requires to supernaturaly manipulate the actual supply chain, it seems. Even when the Syndicate doesn't need any further magick to make the trucks arrive when he wants, nor deal with the paperwork<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I brought up HAB vs. HOO: the latter assumes that every detail has been nailed down; the former doesn't. </div> </div> </div>No. HOO doesn't assume that every detail has been nailed down, because in that case no ST would ever have defended such a preposeterous idea.<br /> <br /> HAP and HOO asumes there is an observer for your actions. HAP assumes it's an average person, that could be anywhere a normal person could be in the scene . HOO asumes it's capable of observing anything it could potentially be observed, even if that observation would require to manipulate the scene with instruments (or perhaps even when it would be impossible for humans - but very few would go so far)<br /> <br /> There are different takes for both. For instance, I think the HAP can see behind the corners, because an average person isn't going to be fiddling with your pockets but could easily be hanging arround at that corner.<br /> <br /> Neither say much about the world, nor the Spheres needed to cast an Effect. In fact, they kinda <i>deny </i>the world.HAP, for instance, says that summoning a tiger from thin air it's Vulgar (in general). But what if I first put the ligths off?, a normal person can't see the tiger being summoned<i> in the dark</i>, is it Coincidental?.<br /> Usually HAP proponents deny these kind of &quot;gotcha&quot;. Because HAP and HOO aren't intended to be strict rules, but mere examples - such an obvious &quot;gotcha&quot; as turning the lights off, probably it's not what Paradox rules talk about when they talk about possible and impossible.<br /> <br /> Here's when &quot;plausible&quot; matters - but ultimately it's not a construction of the world: If there were news of an escaped tiger in the locale, <i>perhaps </i>it could be Coincidental to summon one in the dark. But if you do that with Prime+Life, that's not going to be the <i>same </i>tiger, that <s>teleported here w/o Corr</s> <i>might</i> have been nearby. It's going to be a new tiger, because you <i>created </i>it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's rather obvious that not every detail it's ever set, but the fact that you're purposely tailoring these &quot;unknown&quot; details to make Sindicate magick (and no other) Coincidental, it's something I really don't like<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448418#post1448418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the syndicate agent flatlining someones worth so badly they cease to exist. This is ENTIRELY possible, but its not prime, its entropy and prime. The syndicate agent bankrupts them, fires them, just generally flatlines everything about their value and then lets fate take the wheel. The poor target, homeless, friendless, jobless, then meets their end in some sad fashion. Maybe they take an overdose, maybe they die of grief, maybe they take their own life. Maybe they live but just cease to be relevant to power and worth. Maybe they become a permanent member of the homeless population, maybe they just wander off and are never heard from again. To the syndicate agent, they have been destroyed, the details aren't important. Note that I think this is only really possible with entropy which explicitly allows some form of flexibility between intention and outcome. But entropy seems like such a key sphere for syndicate workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this rework of the extremely bizarre take Syndicate <i>revised </i>had on PU5.<br /> <br /> Notably, Entropy was their main sphere before the (admittedly, rather interesting) changes to Prime. It was the market manipulation Sphere back then. Of course: When Entropy it's a thing, luck it's a thing - call it <i>probability</i>.<br /> <br /> I just don't think the ST should provide a free narrative conceit. I tend to think the scene isn't a self contained bubble in a cosmos of chaos (well, usually) - things and people are assumed to exist outside the scene, and thus you would have to <i>order </i>the trucks of your company to follow you arround (or similar) for me to take seriously the chance of one being near (and, even then, I may chose to flip a coin - they're not going to be near just because you casted a spell. Unless it was magick to make that happen. Not if I go with a &quot;PBD&quot; based approach)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:26:04-07:00","id":1448444,"title":"","content":"It seems you need to be very attentive to your surroundings, if you go against the Syndicate, to avoid them calling on their ST fiat superpowers. A Corr spell to watch the surrounding area could be useful for more than to avoid ambushes, it's also liable to gain you at least one turn before Syndicate summoners do their thing, if the truck has to appear at the <i>end</i> of your perception - obviously, the ST will be <i>told</i> that the character it's looking for machines, because we know our &quot;Human Resources&quot; exploits<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could even shoot the materialization down before it arrives...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:37:48-07:00","id":1448445,"title":"","content":"Okay, me is dumb and you am genius. Happy now?<br /> <br /> Or rather, could you please contain your contempt to one post at a time, and give people a chance to respond before your next ridicule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:45:28-07:00","id":1448446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448445#post1448445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, me is dumb and you am genius. Happy now?<br /> <br /> Or rather, could you please contain your contempt to one post at a time, and give people a chance to respond before your next ridicule?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm going to be happy if you explicitly ditch PBD. Why it's this idea <i>so bad</i>?. Think about it: All Mages can do these things, it's not just the Syndicate or those with <i>Syndicate-like</i> Instruments - but the Syndicate can be the <i>masters </i>of doing this<br /> <br /> I'm extremely unhappy whenever only the Technocracy get's to do RBD. Canon or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:46:32-07:00","id":1448447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448428#post1448428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where I'm coming from with this is that in many cases, Coincidental Magick is to Mage as Dramatic Editing is to the Trinity Continuum or Twists of Fate are to Scion. In each of these cases, the reality that you're dealing with is more cinematic than realistic. You can see this in M20, where the Technocracy's counterpart to mythic threads are the hypernarratives: basically, if it's a \u201cmovie reality\u201d thing, them you get -1 Difficulty on your working for tapping into a hypernarrative. Coincidental Effects that actually represent the kinds of coincidences that make up such a big part of cinematic reality are part and parcel to this.<br /> <br /> And you keep reading \u201cmight have been\u201d as \u201cwasn't, until the mage changed things\u201d. That's specifically <i>not</i> what I'm talking about. The Storyteller can't be expected to pre-establish every detail about the scene and the surrounding environment; so a lot of details (such as whether or not there are any delivery trucks nearby) <i>aren't known by anyone</i>, because the Storyteller didn't nail them down. And <i>that's</i> where the convenient delivery truck resides: in those details that haven't been specified. That's why I brought up HAB vs. HOO: the latter assumes that every detail has been nailed down; the former doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't agree with this. For several reasons.<br /> <br /> This is a power I already give my players in every RPG I run. The world can't be fully defined to us and so we can fill in unestablished yet reasonable things about the world (subject to veto). To give this ability over to Coincidental Magic I have to take away narrative control from the players and I see no reason to do that.<br /> <br /> The ambiguity and gaps that you are exploiting are general elements of shared storytelling, not properties of the world of Mage. Just because we <i>as the players</i> don't know what is in the blank spots doesn't mean they are undefined in universe. The truck driver knows whether he's there or not, as does the hypothetical observer.<br /> <br /> I realize there's not much mechanical difference between the players deciding there is a nearby truck and the spell deciding there is a nearby truck, but from a gaming standpoint the difference is vast. Mage, to me, is not a game about the characters realizing they are in a story and magic is not the process of them exploiting the limitations of the storytellers. <br /> <br /> As for coincidental magic, milage may vary, but at least in PBD I consider it to be purely a function of what the observer will accept. I realize there are examples of coincidental magic where the mage just lets the spell loose to figure out how to resolve coincidentally, but 1) I've always seen those as RBD examples, and 2) I don't think that works under many paradigms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:53:23-07:00","id":1448448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448446#post1448446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm going to be happy if you explicitly ditch PBD. Why it's this idea <i>so bad</i>?. Think about it: All Mages can do these things, it's not just the Syndicate or those with <i>Syndicate-like</i> Instruments - but the Syndicate can be the <i>masters </i>of doing this<br /> <br /> I'm extremely unhappy whenever only the Technocracy get's to do RBD. Canon or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: did you bother to check see whether or not I was ever supporting PBD?<br /> <br /> You have been making unfounded assumptions left and right here. Please stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T12:29:33-07:00","id":1448452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448447#post1448447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for coincidental magic, milage may vary, but at least in PBD I consider it to be purely a function of what the observer will accept. I realize there are examples of coincidental magic where the mage just lets the spell loose to figure out how to resolve coincidentally, but 1) I've always seen those as RBD examples, and 2) I don't think that works under many paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I've been noodling around with the beginnings of an idea for allowing both PBD and RBD in the game, possibly in a manner vaguely similar to C20's Cantrips vs. Unleashing, with each approach having benefits that the other lacks: for instance, PBD allowing you to have more control over the outcome while RBD has fewer requirements that need to be met. Then leave it up to the individual mage to decide which one fits her style of magick better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T12:33:45-07:00","id":1448453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448448#post1448448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: did you bother to check see whether or not I was ever supporting PBD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought I did. Obviously failed to do it properly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence <b>why I stress so much this PBD thing</b>. What changes here isn't Coincidence, but rather the Spheres and successes needed to cast an Effect (in a Coincidental way).<br /> <br /> <b>I need to know, as a player, that these things are viable</b> ways to gain the advantages of Coincidence, and<b> M20 certainly doesn't point me towards that with that PBD section</b>. <i>Less so </i>because it's HAP - <b>hence I think it matters to say: &quot;Yeah, I don't quite agree with M20 stance here&quot;</b>. That way I'm not going to think I can't do the taxicab teleport just because I lack the Spheres to summon an actual, <i>meaningful</i>, taxi</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm such an ass about this, it's not because I have a strong stance on PDB vs RDB, but rather because I think one should be very explicit about this - because it changes things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T05:01:57-07:00","id":1448496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448452#post1448452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I've been noodling around with the beginnings of an idea for allowing both PBD and RBD in the game, possibly in a manner vaguely similar to C20's Cantrips vs. Unleashing, with each approach having benefits that the other lacks: for instance, PBD allowing you to have more control over the outcome while RBD has fewer requirements that need to be met. Then leave it up to the individual mage to decide which one fits her style of magick better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've run into the idea before, it's workable if everyone is on board. The major advantage is it gives a sense that magic (or I suppose Avatars) are alive and active and it represents what some paradigms do in practice if not on paper. The major disadvantage is it creates extra work at the table and a potential mechanical disparity. It also draws a the spheres (as rules) and the spheres (as in universe things) closer together. It's personal preference whether that is a pro or a con.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't work with my playstyle, though. When players try to get me to do more work I often offload it back onto them, so if an undefined spell like that came up I would often just have them brainstorm the way it turned out. That would give players almost the same level of control over RBD spells as PBD spells with significantly less cost. It just wouldn't have the desired effect in my case.<br /> <br /> My method for adjudicating unconsciously cast magic is that the character may not know how the magic is happening but the player does so the same spheres are used. That's the method I would use for magic that is consciously cast but without specific direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T12:33:04-07:00","id":1448613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448337#post1448337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Nasally voice* Well technically the HAN is just an annoyingly perceptive HAB. He can't be a HOO because he can't see inside pockets unless the camera is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say more like &quot;HAN&quot; is a self-styled &quot;HOO&quot;, who gets mad when results don't match expectation. Or to point it more pointedly, when the writers and director of a particular work aren't as &quot;detail-minded&quot; as the viewer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> (That said, I find the way this is implemented in M20 to be kind of clunky, and house-rule it to be a matter of whether your source of power is internal or external rather than mystical or technomantic; and with external sources resulting in Instruments that never go away but which ultimately have greater aptitude with their use, while internal sources let you Work Without Focus and surpass your Instruments as your Arete increases, but has less altitude with Instruments than external sources have.) </div> </div> </div>Except that all paradigms are socially-constructed, and therefore external by definition. Even in the case of orphans, whose paradigms are constructed not as the result of training but organically-developed as the result of societal norms, values, and beliefs. There are no truly &quot;internal&quot; paradigms; no, not even Akashics are free of the influence of external stimuli and influence, and they're those whose paradigm is based on the core concept reality is illusory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> The truck it's part of the delivery service. But , of course, the agent doesn't need the truck to be there - a phonecall it's enough. What's suspicious it's that the magick <i>includes </i>the truck being there </div> </div> </div>I doubt anybody would bat an eye at this sub-topic had our hypothetical Syndicate mage simply used Entropy (the convention's <i>other</i> specialty sphere) 2 or 3 to decide writ nothing the exact object they needed was about to be mistakenly delivered to them via the exact same courier service, at exactly the time they needed it. The notion of whether this object existed at all, regardless of price, rarity, its constituent components, whether the delivery service had it in stock, or associated quintessence cost, would barely be an afterthought if at all.<br /> <br /> Oh, maybe the number of successes the mage needed might be fertile field for discussion, but whether the mage could do it coincidentally or without violating the boundaries of their paradigm wouldn't be up for debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-15-2021, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T04:48:00-07:00","id":1448841,"title":"","content":"The thing is, serendipitous developments shouldn't be restricted to Entropy; <i>any</i> Sphere ought to be able to arrange for them, as Coincidencal Magick. Granted, this would involve taking a closer look at just what Entropy does and doesn't cover, since \u201chappenstance\u201d <i>isn't</i> uniquely its thing. And once you've clarified exactly what Entropy <i>is</i> about, you might want to rethink whether or not it still makes sense as something that the Syndicate focuses on. <br /> <br /> In keeping with the idea that there's overlap between the various Spheres, a lot of what Entropy does is stuff that I wouldn't have a problem with Time or Correspondence/Data doing, too. Heck, even the \u201ccause things to break down\u201d kinds of Effects are the sort of thing that Prime/Primal Utility seems to be able to pull off, in that removing value from something has an effect on it that's not unlike decay. <br /> <br /> As I see it, Entropy as a Sphere may not have <i>anything</i> unique to it, with its <i>raison d'etre</i> being more about convenience (i.e., getting this specific combination of Effects for the cost of raising one Sphere instead of raising two or three other Spheres that do a lot of things you <i>aren't</i> interested in as well as the handful of things you <i>do</i> want) than it is about providing access to powers that you can't get any other way. The Syndicate in particular probably has more interest in Data and Time as ways of manipulating the odds and predicting/shaping the future than with the rather esoteric blend that Entropy represents. If I had to rank the top three Spheres for the Syndicate to focus on, they would be Primal Utility, Data, and Time, in that order. <br /> <br /> Of course, part of this is that I generally <i>don't</i> view Correspondence (and <i>especially</i> not Data) as being primarily about spatial relationships. To me, Corr/Data is primarily about the formal sciences such as mathematics, with the spatial elements being practical manifestations of geometry. Where it overlaps with Entropy is that another area that Correspondence ought to cover would be system theory: the ability to treat things like ecosystems, weather systems, or networks (both digital and personal) as \u201cthings\u201d in their own right. Accessing Primal Ventures should be a Primal Utility/Data conjunctional Effect, not purely (or even primarily) Primal Utility: Data to treat an organization as a thing, and Primal Utility to extract Value from it. <br /> <br /> Another area where I see considerable overlap between Data and Entropy is with Chaos Theory and Statistics: complex systems with many moving parts where a minor change to initial conditions can snowball into vastly different outcomes. Data shouldn't be as good at such such things as Entropy is; it should require more dots and/or possibly a conjunctional use of Time. But it <i>should</i> be doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T06:17:22-07:00","id":1448849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448841#post1448841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, serendipitous developments shouldn't be restricted to Entropy...<i>any</i> Sphere ought to be able to arrange for them, as Coincidencal Magick...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's why I brought it up. And the converse should be true as well; &quot;random chance&quot; oughtn't not be considered a &quot;get out of vulgarity free&quot; card by default, though that's a smoother conversation to be had than the immediate topic. But, this branches deeper into the conversation whether Entropy should exist in its current form at all that's been had before, that's not particularly relevant to the precise topic at hand.<br /> <br /> More to the point, this is there paradigm, tools, and foci begin to overlap with sphere usage and effect for technomages. We're getting into technomages' iteration of &quot;do mages who use chi as a focus need Prime?&quot;. You're quick to point out the correlation between the Data sphere and specific uses of Entropy or Primal Utility within the constraints of certain paradigms; I'll be just as quick to point out the correlation between <i>Forces</i> and that instrumentality of the Data sphere, because ultimately in the context of digital computing that data is expressed and transferred exclusively via electromagnetism. Quantum computing is neither reprieve nor relief of that necessity, because quantum computing raises the specter of needing Forces <i>and</i> Entropy due to Entropy's purview over quantum state, entanglement, superposition, and wave function within a technomagical paradigm (see the VE's splatbook for details).<br /> <br /> I ran into this issue myself when I recently created an Etherite whose paradigm was founded in the many worlds interpretation of quantum physics. And, his major spheres were indeed Entropy, Forces, and Data, in that order with a <i>minor</i> investment into Time.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, in this example a Syndicate mage's usage of databases, spreadsheets, statistical calculations, projections, and predictions based upon the data at hand would be <i>focus</i>, not expression of a sphere in and of itself. They shouldn't need Entropy, Data, or Time to use those tools, in the exact way an Akashic shouldn't need Prime, or a Taftani shouldn't need Spirit, to simply throw a fireball provided they have Forces 2 or 3 to begin with. Do those spheres <i>correlate</i> to the practice, would they be immeasurably helpful to a mage with a corresponding paradigm, or is a mage with that paradigm highly likely to raise their dots in those spheres? absolutely, in all cases. But should it be <i>necessary</i> in the sense that, without those spheres at a largely arbitrary rating, a mage simply cannot use magic at all? absolutely <i>not</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T07:19:58-07:00","id":1448855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448849#post1448849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But ultimately, in this example a Syndicate mage's usage of databases, spreadsheets, statistical calculations, projections, and predictions based upon the data at hand would be <i>focus</i>, not expression of a sphere in and of itself. They shouldn't need Entropy, Data, or Time to use those tools, in the exact way an Akashic shouldn't need Prime, or a Taftani shouldn't need Spirit, to simply throw a fireball provided they have Forces 2 or 3 to begin with. Do those spheres <i>correlate</i> to the practice, would they be immeasurably helpful to a mage with a corresponding paradigm, or is a mage with that paradigm highly likely to raise their dots in those spheres? absolutely, in all cases. But should it be <i>necessary</i> in the sense that, without those spheres at a largely arbitrary rating, a mage simply cannot use magic at all? absolutely <i>not</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, indeed the same effect should be the same spheres in all paradigms. The key, then, is if it is the same effect. Since you mention fireball spells, here's an example I removed from a previous post:<br /> <br /> The standard fireball (without a preexisting source) is Forces 3 Prime 2 and it doesn't stop being that just because of variations of paradigm or theme. A psychic who uses pyrokinesis to hurl fire from his hands isn't doing anything different from a wizard who shoots it from his wand. Mental powers may be the paradigm but no Mind effects are taking place. This remains true even if the paradigm changes the motif or the character of the spell. A shaman who channels the power of a spirit into a single fireball could also use the same spheres and would not have to add Spirit to the mix. She could probably cast an extremely similar effect with Spirit, of course, but if she chooses the Forces, Prime route the spell would not additionally require Spirit, even if the fireball has eyes and a glimmer of personality. Same for a mage who has an angel appear, throw a fireball, and disappear just as quickly. <br /> <br /> On the other hand a Mage who initiates a fireball by having a huge dragon strafe by needs more than Forces and Prime. It is a different effect. The dragon is far more than an incidental element of the fireball itself and bringing it into the scene requires something extra. That remains true even if the Dragon is conveniently already around the corner.<br /> <br /> That's how I approach bringing the truck in. It is too big an effect on the scene to count as incidental for a small item teleport so it needs to be accounted for. Making it (and the corresponding rerouting of transportation networks) part of the foci is one way of doing that. Barring that the spell needs to include a way of bringing in the truck (and presumably driver).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T08:13:48-07:00","id":1448863,"title":"","content":"That said, that \u201csomething extra\u201d shouldn't require you to determine ahead of time whether or not there's a truck nearby to decide whether you're simply locating something that might possibly already be there or you're creating something out of nothing. That is, you shouldn't have to get the Storyteller's approval ahead of time to summon a delivery truck if there's a reasonable chance that there's already a delivery truck: you should be able to just assume that there is one nearby, unless and until the Storyteller overrules you. <br /> <br /> And yes, some of the terminology I'm using there is fuzzy. That's to be expected in a game where units of time are measured in scenes and game sessions. Reality Zones don't have robustly established borders beyond \u201cthey're the stage upon which the current scene plays out\u201d. And so on. Leave the seconds, minutes, hours, yards, miles, and percent chances to games like GURPS; Mage operates on a much more freeform basis. <br /> <br /> But ultimately, there's a big difference between \u201cuse a few dots of Correspondence to contact a local delivery truck\u201d and \u201cuse Prime 2 plus mastery of Matter, Life, Mind, and possibly other Spheres to create a delivery truck and its driver out of thin air\u201d. It's worth noting that Syndics wouldn't even attempt the latter, and not just because of the extreme Sphere requirements. <br /> <br /> And <i>that</i>, in turn, brings us back to the question of whether those Sphere requirements <i>should</i> be so extreme. As Theodrim has pointed out, and which I also indicated above, Mage doesn't operate on a simulationist model; it works more on a narrative basis. If a character shows up who is only going to be incidental to the scene \u2014 what cinema calls an \u201cextra\u201d, you shouldn't have to go with mastery of multiple Spheres to summon him just because he <i>might</i> turn out to be more important than that. And the mage who summons a delivery truck as a piece of mobile scenery with the intent of stealing it and thus making it far more important than he purportedly intended it to be is acting in bad faith \u2014 something that is a \u201cgaming contract\u201d issue rather than a \u201cgame systems\u201d issue. Mages shouldn't be unduly curtailed in what their magical can do just because a jerk might choose to abuse the group's trust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T09:26:32-07:00","id":1448875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448863#post1448863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, that \u201csomething extra\u201d shouldn't require you to determine ahead of time whether or not there's a truck nearby to decide whether you're simply locating something that might possibly already be there or you're creating something out of nothing. That is, you shouldn't have to get the Storyteller's approval ahead of time to summon a delivery truck if there's a reasonable chance that there's already a delivery truck: you should be able to just assume that there is one nearby, unless and until the Storyteller overrules you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very much in agreement with this. I think it applies regardless of if the nearby truck is brought in by magical or mundane means. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But ultimately, there's a big difference between \u201cuse a few dots of Correspondence to contact a local delivery truck\u201d and \u201cuse Prime 2 plus mastery of Matter, Life, Mind, and possibly other Spheres to create a delivery truck and its driver out of thin air\u201d. It's worth noting that Syndics wouldn't even attempt the latter, and not just because of the extreme Sphere requirements. </div> </div> </div>I doubt many mages would. It would take a special kind of thought process to do something so vulgar to facilitate the coincidental summoning of a small item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And <i>that</i>, in turn, brings us back to the question of whether those Sphere requirements <i>should</i> be so extreme. As Theodrim has pointed out, and which I also indicated above, Mage doesn't operate on a simulationist model; it works more on a narrative basis. If a character shows up who is only going to be incidental to the scene \u2014 what cinema calls an \u201cextra\u201d, you shouldn't have to go with mastery of multiple Spheres to summon him just because he <i>might</i> turn out to be more important than that. And the mage who summons a delivery truck as a piece of mobile scenery with the intent of stealing it and thus making it far more important than he purportedly intended it to be is acting in bad faith \u2014 something that is a \u201cgaming contract\u201d issue rather than a \u201cgame systems\u201d issue. Mages shouldn't be unduly curtailed in what their magical can do just because a jerk might choose to abuse the group's trust. </div> </div> </div>Well the requirements should only be extreme if the methods are. Since you bring up gaming contracts, I'm certainly not going to trap a player into casting a spell they weren't intending to. If they try to maneuver a nearby truck into position and I decide there isn't a truck nearby I'm not going to force them to create one whole cloth or lose their turn. The entire idea of letting players assume elements of the world heavily implies that there is a safety net if their assumption is vetoed.<br /> <br /> If they do decide to create one whole cloth, though, it is going to require mastery of multiple spheres regardless of if the truck driver is an extra or not. It isn't curtailing anyone's powers to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-18-2021, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T10:37:58-07:00","id":1448877,"title":"","content":"So I've put forward my thoughts on how a prime 2 matter whatever \u201ccreate an object\u201d effect should be done in the Syndicate Focus, and it has been\u2026 controversial. So let me turn this around: how would you do it? If any decent alternatives have been suggested, I don't remember them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T11:26:29-07:00","id":1448885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1444503-can-someone-explain-to-me-the-syndicate-paradigm-of-primal-utility?p=1448877#post1448877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've put forward my thoughts on how a prime 2 matter whatever \u201ccreate an object\u201d effect should be done in the Syndicate Focus, and it has been\u2026 controversial. So let me turn this around: how would you do it? If any decent alternatives have been suggested, I don't remember them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The methods you've mentioned work great for the Syndicate. The only controversy, at least on my end, has been with specific, non-pivotal (and non syndicate specific) elements of implementation. That has nothing to do with their suitability as effects.<br /> <br /> The only one I would add is the one I mentioned before: commerce and spreadsheet based reality hacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}